var e=[{slug:`deku-tree`,title:`Inside the Deku Tree`,subtitle:`The forest calls your name.`,description:`Find the remake’s raised Kokiri Sword chest, learn the Slingshot puzzles and descend to Gohma.`,era:`Child Link`,reward:`Fairy Slingshot · Kokiri's Emerald`,category:`story`,prerequisites:[`A new Nintendo Switch 2 remake save`],steps:[{id:`sword-shield`,title:`Equip a sword and shield`,text:`From Link’s house, visit the training grounds and practise the dodges. Crawl through the low opening into the boulder area. Follow the moving boulder safely, climb the ladder and jump to the raised chest for the Kokiri Sword. Gather 40 Rupees, buy the Deku Shield at the village shop and return to Mido with both equipped.`,evidence:[`sword`,`shield`,`respec`]},{id:`slingshot`,title:`Climb to the slingshot`,text:`Enter the tree and climb the lobby vines. Follow the walkway past the map chest. In the side room, raise your shield to reflect the Deku Scrub’s shot, then speak to it. Cross the collapsing walkway to the Fairy Slingshot chest; climb the vines if you fall. Shoot the eye above the exit to lower the ladder.`,evidence:[`space4`,`retro`,`respec`]},{id:`upper-floor`,title:`Reach the highest walkway`,text:`Back in the lobby, shoot the Skullwalltulas before climbing the tall vines. Hit a hanging Skulltula to make it expose its underside, then strike the soft belly. In the Compass room, press the switch to raise the platforms. The left alcove contains a Gold Skulltula; the far chest holds the Compass. No torch is needed to leave.`,evidence:[`retro`,`space4`]},{id:`break-web`,title:`Break the floor web`,text:`Jump from the upper walkway toward the middle of the web far below. A properly centered landing tears it and drops you into the basement. Step on the basement switch to light the protected torch.`,evidence:[`space4`,`retro`,`respec`]},{id:`first-fire`,title:`Carry fire across the water`,text:`Light a Deku Stick at that torch. Use the shallow section of water to reach the web-covered doorway without submerging the flame, then touch the web with the stick. Deflect the next Scrub's nut and hear its clue. Shoot the eye above the next door.`,evidence:[`space4`,`retro`,`respec`]},{id:`water-switch`,title:`Pass beneath the spiked roller`,text:`Dive onto the underwater switch to lower the water. Return to the starting side and ride the moving platform beneath the thorned roller. Go through the far door. In the following chamber, defeat the Skulltula, move the block beneath the ledge and climb onward.`,evidence:[`retro`,`space4`]},{id:`return-ledge`,title:`Reach the upper basement ledge`,text:`Light all the unlit torches with a burning Deku Stick. Beyond the next spider and Gohma Larvae, burn both webs. The side cave contains the fourth Gold Skulltula, reachable now with the Slingshot and vines. The other route leads through a crawlspace back to the upper basement ledge. Push its block down.`,evidence:[`retro`,`space4`,`respec`]},{id:`second-web`,title:`Burn the second floor web`,text:`Get fire from the basement torch and climb back using the moved block. Swing the burning stick into the floor web to ignite it, then drop into the lower room.`,evidence:[`retro`,`respec`]},{id:`scrub-code`,title:`Use the Scrubs' order`,text:`Reflect nuts at the three Scrubs in this order: middle, right, left. Chase and speak to the final Scrub to unlock the boss chamber. Enter and look up to begin the encounter.`,evidence:[`space4`,`retro`,`respec`]},{id:`emerald`,title:`Return with the Emerald`,text:`After defeating Gohma, take the Heart Container and enter the blue light. Listen to the Deku Tree and receive Kokiri's Emerald. Leave the forest by its western exit; Saria gives you the Fairy Ocarina on the bridge.`,evidence:[`space4`,`fairy-ocarina`,`respec`]}],boss:{name:`Gohma`,strategy:[`Keep her eye in view. Shoot with the Slingshot when the pincers uncover it, then close in and strike the eye while she is stunned.`,`A Slingshot hit on the exposed ceiling eye knocks her down. If she lays eggs, break them before they hatch; clear any larvae and return to the eye.`]},notes:[`The reading checklist and your game save are separate.`,`Published remake guides disagree on whether the roller-room water rises again. Cross promptly; this route does not depend on a claimed timer.`],changes:[`The Kokiri Sword is reached by a ladder and jump to an elevated chest.`,`The Slingshot exit uses an eye switch; the Compass-room exit no longer needs a lit torch.`,`All four dungeon Gold Skulltulas can be collected on this first visit.`],sources:[{id:`respec`,label:`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested Switch 2 walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`space4`,label:`SPACE4GAMES · Josef Erl · own Switch 2 playthrough`,href:`https://space4games.com/en/games-en/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-great-deku-tree-walkthrough/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`retro`,label:`Retro Dodo · Sebastian Santabarbara · remake dungeon changes`,href:`https://retrododo.com/inside-the-great-deku-tree-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`sword`,label:`Retro Dodo · the remake Kokiri Sword puzzle`,href:`https://retrododo.com/how-to-get-your-first-sword-in-ocarina-of-time/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`shield`,label:`Retro Dodo · Deku Shield and child equipment`,href:`https://retrododo.com/how-to-get-your-first-shield-in-ocarina-of-time-remake/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`fairy-ocarina`,label:`Retro Dodo · Saria and the Fairy Ocarina`,href:`https://retrododo.com/how-to-get-your-first-ocarina-in-ocarina-of-time-remake/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`princess-and-gorons`,title:`The princess & the Gorons`,subtitle:`A song can open a kingdom.`,description:`Sneak through the new castle approach, meet Zelda and prepare the route to Dodongo Cavern.`,era:`Child Link`,reward:`Zelda's Letter · two songs · Goron's Bracelet`,category:`story`,prerequisites:[`Kokiri's Emerald`,`Fairy Ocarina`],steps:[{id:`market`,title:`Travel to Hyrule Castle`,text:`Cross Hyrule Field toward Hyrule Castle Town, then follow the road uphill to the castle. Speak to Malon beside the milk cart and agree to find her father. She gives you a Weird Egg. The Potion Shop’s bug-catching request in town also gives you a useful extra bottle.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`talon`,title:`Wake the sleeping rancher`,text:`Climb the vines behind Malon and get beyond the gate. Use the tall hedges as cover and climb the vines at the end of the route. Swim along the moat, past the entrance bridge and around the corner to Talon. Once the egg hatches, equip the Wake-Up Cucco and use it beside him.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`courtyard`,title:`Reach Zelda's courtyard`,text:`Move the crates Talon left behind to make a step up to the drain opening. Crawl through. In the castle grounds, wait for guards to turn away before crossing and use the scenery as cover. Continue through the indoor patrol to Zelda’s courtyard. Speak to Zelda, accept her request and take her Letter. Impa teaches Zelda’s Lullaby before escorting you out.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`saria`,title:`Visit Saria in the Sacred Forest Meadow`,text:`Return to Kokiri Forest and enter the Lost Woods. From the entrance, take right, left, right, left, straight, left, right. Follow the music and the flowing green notes at the correct tunnels. Defeat the Wolfos, pass the Mad Scrubs with your shield raised and climb to Saria to learn Saria’s Song.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`suns-song`,title:`Learn the Sun’s Song`,text:`At the back of Kakariko Graveyard, stand on the Triforce before the Royal Family’s Tomb and play Zelda’s Lullaby. Enter the opened crypt, defeat the bats, pass the ReDeads and read the inscription at the end to learn the Sun’s Song. It changes day and night and stuns ReDeads.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`shield`,title:`Get the Hylian Shield`,text:`The wooden shield burns in fire. Buy a Hylian Shield in Castle Town, or collect the free one in Kakariko Graveyard: learn the Sun’s Song in the Royal Family’s Tomb, make it night and pull the second grave to the right of the path when facing the royal tomb. Below, stun the ReDead with the Sun’s Song, defeat it and open the chest.`,evidence:[`respec`,`shield`]},{id:`gate`,title:`Open the Death Mountain gate`,text:`At Kakariko’s northern gate, show Zelda’s Letter to the guard. With the gate open, follow Death Mountain Trail uphill to Goron City.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`darunia`,title:`Play for Darunia`,text:`Descend to Goron City's lowest level. Play Zelda's Lullaby on the mat in front of Darunia's door. Inside, speak to him and play Saria's Song. He gives the Goron's Bracelet, which lets child Link lift Bomb Flowers.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`cavern`,title:`Unblock Dodongo's Cavern`,text:`Exit Goron City to the mountain trail. At the nearby fenced ledge, lift a Bomb Flower and throw it down toward the giant boulder sealing the cavern below. Reposition and repeat if it misses. Descend the path and enter the opened cavern.`,evidence:[`respec`]}],notes:[`Lon Lon Ranch’s bottle and Epona’s Song are optional here; collect them before following the horse quest later.`,`The Happy Mask trade does not block these story steps.`],changes:[`Malon waits beside a milk cart; the hatched Wake-Up Cucco wakes Talon.`,`The free Hylian Shield is in a ReDead tomb, not the old flower-marked-grave shorthand.`,`Green musical notes now help identify the correct Lost Woods tunnels.`],sources:[{id:`respec`,label:`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested Switch 2 walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`shield`,label:`Retro Dodo · Deku Shield and child equipment`,href:`https://retrododo.com/how-to-get-your-first-shield-in-ocarina-of-time-remake/`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`dodongos-cavern`,title:`Dodongo's Cavern`,subtitle:`There is a heartbeat beneath the mountain.`,description:`Use Bomb Flowers and eye switches to get the Bomb Bag, defeat King Dodongo and unlock Din’s Fire.`,era:`Child Link`,reward:`Bomb Bag · Goron’s Ruby · magic meter · Din’s Fire · enhanced Spin Attack`,category:`story`,prerequisites:[`Goron's Bracelet`,`Slingshot`,`Deku Sticks`,`Hylian Shield recommended`],steps:[{id:`lobby`,title:`Open the cavern`,text:`Use the entrance Bomb Flower to destroy the cracked wall. In the main lava hall, cross to the west side and bomb the northwestern alcove for the map. Cross to the east side; bomb the southern alcove to open the route onward. The northern eastern alcove contains a Gossip Stone.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`east-switch`,title:`Clear the eastern loop`,text:`Pass the Baby Dodongos and stay clear after striking them: they explode. Push the statue onto the floor switch. Defeat both Lizalfos. In the next passages, use Bomb Flowers against the Dodongos, then carry a burning Deku Stick to the unlit torches. Return to the main hall and press the switch that opens the western route.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`stairs`,title:`Drop the enormous staircase`,text:`Cross the lobby to the newly opened west door. In the room lined with Bomb Flowers, place one flower in the empty gap between the two rows. The simultaneous chain explosion lowers the staircase. Climb it.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`bridge`,title:`Cross above the lobby`,text:`At the top of the staircase, clear or avoid the Armos statues and move the one blocking the ladder. Climb to the switch. Cross the high bridge above the main hall, then continue to the block-and-platform room.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`timed-bomb`,title:`Break the high wall`,text:`Pull the block beneath the ladder and climb to the platforms. From the Bomb Flower ledge, time a throw so the flower blasts the high cracked wall. Climb through the opening.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`fire-platforms`,title:`Switch off the platform flames`,text:`Shoot the eye above the far door to cross the first flame platform. Defeat the next pair of Lizalfos. In the following room, shoot the first eye, jump to the middle platform and shoot the newly visible side eye to complete the crossing.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`bomb-bag`,title:`Collect the Bomb Bag`,text:`Continue over the upper blade-trap room to the large chest. The Bomb Bag lets you carry and place your own bombs. Step on the nearby switch to extend the lobby elevator.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`eyes`,title:`Light the skull's eyes`,text:`Stand on the bridge above the giant stone skull. Drop one bomb through each of the two openings so it detonates inside an eye socket. When both eyes glow, the mouth opens. Descend and enter it.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`last-block`,title:`Unlock the last door`,text:`From the skull’s mouth, follow the block-puzzle passage. Use the lower block as a foothold to push the upper block down, then move it to reach and shift the block obstructing the route. Drop the final block into its floor slot to open the way to King Dodongo. Continue to the boss chamber. In the final chamber, bomb the cracked floor to open the drop into the arena.`,evidence:[`respec`,`nintenderos`]},{id:`ruby`,title:`Claim the second Spiritual Stone`,text:`Drop into King Dodongo's arena. After the battle, take the Heart Container and blue warp. Darunia gives you Goron's Ruby outside.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`magic`,title:`Visit the mountain Great Fairy`,text:`Climb Death Mountain, using bombs on the rocks that block the way. Shelter beneath the Hylian Shield when rocks fall and climb to the summit. Bomb the cave beside the owl. Play Zelda’s Lullaby at the fountain and make the offering to unlock the magic meter and Din’s Fire.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`dins-fire`,title:`Visit the castle fairy`,text:`Return to the Hyrule Castle approach. Climb past the gate by the vines and bomb the cracked wall nearby. Crawl into the fountain, play Zelda’s Lullaby and pay 50 Rupees. This fairy gives the enhanced Spin Attack; Din’s Fire came from the mountain summit.`,evidence:[`respec`]}],boss:{name:`King Dodongo`,strategy:[`When his mouth opens to inhale, throw a bomb or Bomb Flower inside. Move in and strike while he is stunned.`,`Retreat as he recovers and keep clear of his charge or roll. Stay on solid ground and out of the lava; repeat the bomb-and-sword opening.`]},notes:[`Equip the Hylian Shield before the fiery rooms.`,`Dungeon collectible locations and later revisits are tracked separately from this story route.`],changes:[`The Death Mountain summit fairy now grants Din’s Fire and the magic meter.`,`The Hyrule Castle fairy grants the enhanced Spin Attack for a 50-Rupee offering.`],sources:[{id:`respec`,label:`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested Switch 2 walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`nintenderos`,label:`Nintenderos · Dodongo Cavern remake guide`,href:`https://www.nintenderos.com/2026/11/guia-paso-a-paso-de-la-cueva-de-los-dodongos-en-zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`jabu-jabu`,title:`Inside Jabu-Jabu`,subtitle:`Carry a princess. Trust a boomerang.`,description:`Win the Silver Scale, follow Ruto’s letter and use the Boomerang to rescue her from Jabu-Jabu.`,era:`Child Link`,reward:`Silver Scale · bottle · Boomerang · Zora's Sapphire`,category:`story`,prerequisites:[`Bomb Bag`,`Zelda’s Lullaby`,`Fairy Slingshot`,`Deku Nuts`,`A bottle or the bottle from Ruto’s letter`],steps:[{id:`domain`,title:`Open the waterfall`,text:`Enter Zora’s River from Hyrule Field and bomb the rocks blocking the path. Follow the banks uphill. At the waterfall, stand on the royal crest and play Zelda’s Lullaby, then enter the revealed route to Zora’s Domain.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`letter`,title:`Find Ruto's letter`,text:`From King Zora’s chamber, take the left passage to the diving instructor. Complete his diving game and return for the Silver Scale. Dive through the underwater passage at the bottom of the Domain to Lake Hylia. Retrieve the bottled letter just beyond the tunnel, return to the Domain and show it to King Zora.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`feed`,title:`Enter the guardian`,text:`After the king moves, keep the now-empty bottle. Catch a fish in the shallow water beneath his chamber. Follow the passage behind him to Zora’s Fountain and release the fish into the dish in front of Jabu-Jabu. He draws you inside.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`ruto`,title:`Catch up with Princess Ruto`,text:`Shoot the dangling ceiling switch to open the first door. Stun the jellyfish with a Deku Nut before using your sword. Continue to Ruto and follow her down the hole. Speak to her until she agrees to be carried, then take the nearest door with her.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`carry`,title:`Carry her back upstairs`,text:`In the water room, set Ruto safely down, press the switch to raise the water and collect the map. Return to Ruto to drain the room. Use the low platforms to throw her onto the far ledge, raise the water again and climb up to retrieve her. Shoot the ceiling switch beyond. In the next room, call the elevator with its overhead switch, put Ruto on it and ride up together.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`boomerang`,title:`Use her weight to reach the Boomerang`,text:`Carry Ruto north through the room where you first met her. In the branching corridor, take the right route to the large floor switch. Press it while carrying Ruto, leave her on the switch and enter. Defeat the Stingers to reveal the Boomerang chest.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`tentacles`,title:`Remove the parasitic tentacles`,text:`Use Ruto to hold open the remaining switch-controlled rooms. Defeat the hanging parasites with targeted Boomerang throws. Clear the newly accessible rooms in turn, including the bubble room for the Compass. Cut the blue and green tentacles until the electrical barrier on the route back to the hub disappears.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`bigocto`,title:`Recover the Spiritual Stone`,text:`Pick Ruto up and return to the floor-hole room. Drop through the newly cleared hole. In the next chamber, throw Ruto onto the raised platform. Stun Big Octo with the Boomerang, move behind it to its weak point and attack. Repeat until it falls, then ride the platform that carried Ruto upward.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`moving-platforms`,title:`Cross the trembling platforms`,text:`Go down the ramp and clear the Octorok. Stun the wobbling electrical platforms with the Boomerang before crossing. Continue to the next drop, pick up the stone cube and place it on the floor switch ahead. The switch opens the final passage.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`last-switch`,title:`Curve a throw around the barrier`,text:`In the last room, clear the jellyfish and climb the vine-covered tower. Aim the Boomerang around the transparent barrier to hit the hanging switch: there is no straight shot. Enter Barinade’s room. After winning, take the Heart Container and leave with Ruto to receive Zora’s Sapphire.`,evidence:[`respec`]}],boss:{name:`Barinade`,strategy:[`Keep circling and target the ceiling attachments with the Boomerang until Barinade detaches.`,`Clear the protective jellyfish, then hit the exposed core with the Boomerang. Slash it while it is stunned and back away as the electricity returns.`]},notes:[`If you lose Ruto before the elevator, return to the room where she fell. After the elevator, check the upper room where you first met her.`,`The Zora’s Fountain fairy requires bombs and Zelda’s Lullaby. You may return after the dungeon if you cannot afford the offering.`],changes:[`The early water-room route includes the map before carrying Ruto onward.`,`A stone cube holds the final floor switch; the original wooden-crate instruction does not apply.`,`Farore’s Wind is available from the Zora’s Fountain fairy for 100 Rupees; it is helpful but optional for this dungeon.`],sources:[{id:`respec`,label:`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested Switch 2 walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`door-of-time`,title:`The Door of Time`,subtitle:`Seven years between two breaths.`,description:`Open the Door of Time, meet Rauru and Sheik, then win the Hookshot for the Forest Temple.`,era:`Both ages`,reward:`Master Sword · Light Medallion · Hookshot · Song of Storms`,category:`story`,prerequisites:[`All three Spiritual Stones`,`A bottle recommended`],steps:[{id:`ocarina`,title:`Return to the castle drawbridge`,text:`Approach Castle Town from Hyrule Field. After the escape scene, dive into the moat and retrieve the Ocarina of Time. Zelda's message teaches the Song of Time.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`door`,title:`Open the Door of Time`,text:`Enter the Temple of Time through the path beside the market. Stand before its altar and play the Song of Time. With all three Spiritual Stones collected, the door opens. Enter and pull the Master Sword.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`adult`,title:`Listen to Rauru and Sheik`,text:`The story moves seven years ahead. Rauru gives you the Light Medallion; Sheik explains the temples. Leave through the ruined market and cross the field toward Kakariko Village.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`grave`,title:`Enter Dampe's grave`,text:`Go to Kakariko Graveyard and find the grave near the withered tree and the Magic Bean soil. Pull it back and descend. Speak to Dampé’s ghost and accept his challenge. Follow him closely through the tunnels, keeping up at each fork.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`hookshot`,title:`Take the Hookshot`,text:`Finish the chase and speak to Dampé. Open his chest for the Hookshot. The one-minute challenge is a separate Heart Piece reward. Equip the Hookshot and fire it at the target over the high doorway, then take the stairs to the windmill.`,evidence:[`respec`,`gameplay-dampe`]},{id:`storms`,title:`Remember the windmill's song`,text:`As adult Link, speak to the windmill musician and show him the Ocarina. Repeat the Song of Storms. This creates access to the Bottom of the Well when you revisit Kakariko as a child later.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`meadow`,title:`Find the temple above the meadow`,text:`Return to Kokiri Forest and the Lost Woods. Follow the route toward the Sacred Forest Meadow and play Saria’s Song when Mido blocks your path. Continue through the maze, keeping behind cover and crossing each patrol’s path after it turns away. Reach the clearing above the long stairs.`,evidence:[`respec`]},{id:`minuet`,title:`Learn the Minuet of Forest`,text:`Play the Song of Time in front of the blue stone barrier in the Sacred Forest Meadow. Beyond it, learn the Minuet of Forest from Sheik, then use the Hookshot target above the entrance to reach the Forest Temple.`,evidence:[`respec`,`gameplay-meadow`]}],notes:[`Before drawing the sword, finish any child-era errands you want immediately available. You regain time travel after the Forest Temple.`,`Optional horse and trading quests have separate checklists.`],changes:[`Dampé’s first chase awards the Hookshot; a later run under one minute awards a Heart Piece.`,`Mido has a new scene before opening the way after Saria’s Song.`,`Use the Hookshot to leave Dampé’s tomb. The Song of Time clears the blue barrier on the way to the Forest Temple.`],sources:[{id:`respec`,label:`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested Switch 2 walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`firsthand-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`gameplay-dampe`,label:`Gamer’s Little Playground · Dampé’s exit`,href:`https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oLHiQX2wxrE&t=28693s`,basis:`gameplay`,publishedOn:`2026-11-04`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`gameplay-meadow`,label:`Gamer’s Little Playground · Forest Temple approach`,href:`https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oLHiQX2wxrE&t=30150s`,basis:`gameplay`,publishedOn:`2026-11-04`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]}],t=[{slug:`forest-temple`,title:`Forest Temple`,subtitle:`Four flames. A different way to find the truth.`,description:`Recover the Fairy Bow, reunite the Poe flames and clear the remake’s altered basement.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Hookshot`,`Song of Time`,`Minuet of Forest`],reward:`Fairy Bow · Forest Medallion · travel between ages`,steps:[{id:`forest-temple-tree-key`,title:`Unlock the temple entrance`,text:`Defeat the courtyard Wolfos, climb the vines and cross the branches. Open the tree chest for a Small Key, then spend it on the entrance door. Clear the Skulltula in the passage.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-north-key`,title:`Take the northern Stalfos key`,text:`After the four Poes steal the lobby flames, take the northern stairs and door. Defeat the Blue Bubble, then both Stalfos in the next room. Open their key chest and return to the lobby.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-courtyard-key`,title:`Drain the courtyard well`,text:`Remove the northwest Time Block with the Song of Time. Clear the vine spiders, climb to the balcony and Hookshot across. Step on the switch; descend the drained well for a key. Climb out, Hookshot to the Map chest and use the exit switch to reopen the lobby connection.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-block-room`,title:`Build a path through the block room`,text:`Return to the lobby and unlock the west door. Beyond the Blue Bubble, follow the floor arrows to pull and push the large green block into its socket. Climb up and work around to move the red block into place. Use both as stairs to the upper locked door.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-upper-shortcut`,title:`Activate the upper shortcut`,text:`Climb beyond the two blocks and defeat the Bubbles. Step on the switch that creates an elevator, but keep exploring the upper floor rather than riding down. Unlock the upper door and follow the twisted corridor. Watch for the Wallmaster’s spotlight.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-bow`,title:`Win the Fairy Bow`,text:`Follow the portrait staircase to the arena. Defeat its three Stalfos and open the chest for the Fairy Bow. Shoot the eye above the return door so you can leave.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-untwist`,title:`Untwist the west passage`,text:`Return through the block room to the eye above the twisted corridor entrance. Shoot it to straighten the passage. Cross again: the ornate chest is now reachable and contains the Boss Key. Drop through the nearby floor opening, clear the Bubbles and exit onto an upper courtyard ledge.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-floormaster`,title:`Win the courtyard key`,text:`Enter the small side room off that ledge and defeat its Floormaster, including all three smaller hands before they reunite. Take the Small Key. Return through the courtyard and block room; shoot the eye again to restore the twisted corridor.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-red-poe`,title:`Restore the red flame`,text:`Return to the red portrait staircase. Shoot the occupied paintings from a distance until the Poe leaves them. Fight her below: avoid staring at her while approaching, then attack when she becomes vulnerable. Open her Small Key chest.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-blue-poe`,title:`Restore the blue flame`,text:`Cross the bow arena and unlock the blue wing. Chase the blue Poe out of her paintings and defeat her. Collect the Compass, climb the stairs and follow the upper corridor.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-frozen-eye`,title:`Twist the blue corridor`,text:`In the far room, press the switch to light the torch. Shoot through its flame to melt the frozen eye, then shoot the exposed eye again. Return along the twisted corridor and drop through the floor opening.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-ceiling`,title:`Cross the falling ceiling`,text:`Watch one ceiling cycle before moving. Stand where its holes leave safe spaces, advance to the floor switch and then reach the opened door. Do not stop beneath a solid section of ceiling.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-green-poe`,title:`Rebuild the green portrait`,text:`Shoot the green painting to start the block puzzle. Set the duplicate centre piece aside; arrange the four matching pieces into the complete portrait. Defeat the green Poe, then shoot the final painting and follow its occupant to the lobby.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-meg`,title:`Read Meg’s new clues`,text:`Meg makes four copies. During the first two splits, shoot the copy carrying the purple flame. In the final split, shoot the one with wide-open eyes. Attack her after each correct choice until the fourth flame returns.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-basement`,title:`Open the remake’s basement exit`,text:`Ride the lobby elevator down. Rotate the basement clockwise three times and press the exposed switch. Rotate it clockwise once more. Shoot through the torch flame at the frozen eye beyond the window; shoot the thawed eye again to open the boss route.`,evidence:[`forest-guide`]},{id:`forest-temple-time-travel`,title:`Reopen the path to childhood`,text:`Collect the heart and Forest Medallion after the fight. Return to the Temple of Time. Sheik teaches the Prelude of Light and explains that placing the Master Sword back in its pedestal returns Link to childhood. Pulling it again restores adulthood.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]}],changes:[`The first tree key opens the temple entrance.`,`Meg uses flame and eye clues; the rotating basement now ends with a frozen-eye puzzle.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`This chapter follows the Switch 2 remake, with a separate checklist from the original N64 guide.`],sources:[{id:`forest-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Forest Temple`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-forest-temple-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`boss-guide`,label:`G2A · remake boss mechanics`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-boss-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Phantom Ganon`,strategy:[`Watch the paintings and shoot the real rider as he emerges; his horse sounds help identify him.`,`Return his energy sphere with timed sword swings until it hits him, then close in and strike.`,`When the spear tip flashes before a charge, evade and wait for the next safe opening.`]}},{slug:`fire-temple`,title:`Fire Temple`,subtitle:`Nine prisoners. One very large hammer.`,description:`Free the Gorons, solve the remake’s weighted fire switch and reach Volvagia.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Forest Temple complete`,`Bow`,`Bombs`,`Hookshot`],reward:`Goron Tunic · Megaton Hammer · Fire Medallion`,steps:[{id:`fire-temple-tunic`,title:`Speak to the young Goron`,text:`In adult Goron City, stop the rolling Goron with a bomb. Speak to him about the dragon and the Gorons until he gives you the Goron Tunic. Equip it. Pull the statue in Darunia's room to reveal the crater passage; Hookshot across the broken bridge, learn the Bolero of Fire from Sheik and descend into the temple.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-first-key`,title:`Meet Darunia and free a prisoner`,text:`In the lobby, climb the stairs and enter the left door. After speaking to Darunia, use the platforms on the left to reach a cell switch. Free the Goron and open his chest for a Small Key. Return to the lobby and unlock the right door.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-lava-keys`,title:`Search both ends of the lava chamber`,text:`From the bridge, explore the left-side door for a second prisoner and key. On the opposite side, bomb the cracked wall to find another cell and key. Return to the bridge and unlock the far door.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-fire-lift`,title:`Ride the block above the fire`,text:`Unlock the eastern route and climb the mesh walls. Push the stone block onto the fire jet, stand on it and ride upward. In the Torch Slug room, pull the next block out, toggle the crystal and climb. Shoot the crystal from the upper steps to reopen the climb.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-lower-maze`,title:`Search the lower rolling-orb maze`,text:`Wait for each rolling orb to pass before crossing its track. The short left branch has the Map. Follow the right-hand perimeter to free the next Goron and take its key. Bomb the nearby cracked side wall only if you want its optional token.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-compass`,title:`Open the eye-door branch`,text:`Use a key to enter the central room off the maze. Shoot the eye above the side door and take the Compass beyond it. Return, then use the other passage into the chamber of metal platforms above lava.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-upper-maze`,title:`Return above the maze`,text:`As you step onto the grating, a wall of fire begins following you. Run to the far end, push the red block and enter the upper maze. Rescue the southern Goron for a key. Bomb the central rock pile, descend and rescue another Goron for another key.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-fire-maze`,title:`Hold down the fire-maze switch`,text:`Return to the moving-fire chamber and unlock its middle doorway. Explore the first fire maze’s northern side for another prisoner and key. Cross the locked middle passage. Carry a loose stone cube from the northern corner back onto the floor switch; its weight shuts down the fire traps.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-dancer`,title:`Defeat the first Flare Dancer`,text:`Target the dancer and Hookshot its small core out of the fire, then strike it while it flees. Repeat until it is defeated. Ride the central platform upward. In the next room, activate the crystal switch with a delayed bomb so you can climb the fence while its flames are down.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-hammer`,title:`Race up the rising staircase`,text:`At the top, press the floor switch. Run up the rising spiral staircase before the route retracts and open the Megaton Hammer chest. Retry from the switch if the timer expires.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-hammer-descent`,title:`Drive the platforms downward`,text:`Hammer the circular floor plate and drop with it. Smash the decorated statue, defeat the Keese and pound the next switch to form stairs. Continue through the lower doorway and hammer the next plate. Break the black rocks to reach the Time Block.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-last-small-key`,title:`Free the Goron below`,text:`At the Time Block, play the Song of Time to move it, cross and hammer the rusty switch. Drop to the cell it opens and collect its key. Return above and hammer the large column so it falls into the lava room where Darunia entered the boss door.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-boss-key`,title:`Return to the lobby's ground floor`,text:`Go back to the entrance lobby. Hammer the totem blocking the ground-floor locked door. Clear the enemy rooms, defend against the flying tiles and defeat the second Flare Dancer. Hammer the rusty switch to free the final prisoner and collect the Boss Key.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]},{id:`fire-temple-volvagia`,title:`Cross to Volvagia`,text:`Return to Darunia's lava room by the lobby's upstairs left door. The lowered column now provides a route to the boss door. Win the battle, take the heart and enter the warp for the Fire Medallion.`,evidence:[`fire-guide`]}],changes:[`The lower rolling-orb maze contains the Map; its eye-door branch contains the Compass.`,`A carried stone cube holds the fire-maze switch down.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`The Goron Tunic removes the heat countdown; fire and lava can still hurt you.`],sources:[{id:`fire-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Fire Temple Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-fire-temple-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`boss-guide`,label:`G2A · remake boss mechanics`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-boss-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Volvagia`,strategy:[`Avoid the emerging head’s flame, hammer it and use the stun to land sword strikes.`,`During flight, keep moving away from the breath and falling-rock shadows.`,`Watch for the true emergence hole rather than waiting beside a single hole; repeat the hammer-and-sword opening.`]}},{slug:`ice-cavern`,title:`Ice Cavern`,subtitle:`Carry the blue flame. Read the new crystals.`,description:`Bottle Blue Fire, solve the remake’s sliding-block route and recover the Iron Boots.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`At least one empty bottle`,`Hookshot`,`Bow`,`Song of Time`,`Zelda’s Lullaby`],reward:`Iron Boots · Serenade of Water · Zora Tunic`,steps:[{id:`ice-cavern-icebergs`,title:`Reach the frozen fountain`,text:`Travel up Zora's River and play Zelda's Lullaby at the waterfall. In the frozen domain, go behind King Zora into the fountain. Jump across the ice floes toward the Ice Cavern entrance at the side of the lake.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-first-crystals`,title:`Collect the first five crystals`,text:`Clear the Freezards without standing in their icy breath. In the rotating-blade room, gather the five ice crystals, including the one above the raised ledge. Follow the blade rather than jumping blindly across it. The completed set opens the passage.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-blue-fire`,title:`Bottle blue fire`,text:`In the next chamber, fill an empty bottle from the blue flame. Release it against red ice to melt it; ordinary fire will not substitute. The map chest is beneath red ice here. Refill the bottle before returning to the rotating-blade chamber.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-compass-branch`,title:`Visit the Compass branch`,text:`Return to the rotating blade and melt the red ice in the side branch. Clear the Freezards and Keese, refill Blue Fire and open the Compass chest. Return to the blade room and melt the lower blocked passage toward the sliding block.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-pillar-crystals`,title:`Move the block between the pillars`,text:`Clear the Keese and collect the lowest crystal. Push the sliding block south, west, north, then east, gathering the raised crystals along the way. Next push west, south, west to reach the Blue Fire ledge and refill. Push the block off the edge to reset it.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-last-crystal`,title:`Melt the northern crystal`,text:`Refill Blue Fire at its ledge, resetting the block if necessary. From the starting position, push the block west then north. Climb it, melt the red ice and collect the last crystal to open the exit.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-exit-block`,title:`Place the block below the exit`,text:`Push the block off the edge to reset it. Move the fresh block south, west, north, east, then south. Climb from it into the open passage. Refill Blue Fire and melt the final obstruction on the way to the wolf.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-boots`,title:`Defeat the White Wolfos`,text:`Melt the final red ice in the passage. In the last chamber, guard against the White Wolfos and counterattack after its swipes. Open the chest for the Iron Boots. Sheik teaches the Serenade of Water.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-quick-boots`,title:`Use the Iron Boots shortcut`,text:`Equip the Iron Boots from Equipment. D-pad Down now switches them on and off. Sink through the pool behind the chest and use the underwater exit, then remove them to surface.`,evidence:[`ice-guide`]},{id:`ice-cavern-king-zora`,title:`Thaw King Zora`,text:`Carry a fresh bottle of Blue Fire back to the frozen king. Release it against his red ice and speak to him for the Zora Tunic. Equip the tunic before exploring the Water Temple.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]}],changes:[`The collection puzzles use ice crystals.`,`The old Compass-branch Heart Piece moved; it is not part of this required route.`,`D-pad Down toggles equipped Iron Boots.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`Compass directions below follow the dungeon map, rather than the camera’s current angle.`,`Keep at least one bottle filled with Blue Fire for King Zora.`],sources:[{id:`ice-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Ice Cavern`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-ice-cavern-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`items-guide`,label:`RPG Site · verified remake item locations`,href:`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21671-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-minimalist-100-walkthrough-all-items-gold-skulltula-tokens-heart-pieces`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`water-temple`,title:`Water Temple`,subtitle:`Four required keys. A new duel in the mist.`,description:`Follow the remake’s four-key route, earn the Longshot and defeat Morpha’s expanded phases.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Iron Boots`,`Zora Tunic`,`Hookshot`,`Bow`,`Bombs`,`Zelda’s Lullaby`],reward:`Longshot · Water Medallion · Fire Arrows`,steps:[{id:`water-temple-entry`,title:`Enter beneath Lake Hylia`,text:`Equip the Zora Tunic and Iron Boots. Sink to the underwater doorway below the island and Hookshot its overhead target to open the gate. Inside, surface into the main chamber, then sink to the bottom and take the east passage to Ruto.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-map-low`,title:`Lower the water at Ruto’s crest`,text:`After speaking to Ruto, remove the boots and follow the shaft upward. Take the Map and play Zelda’s Lullaby at the royal crest to lower the water fully. Drop back down into the water below.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-key-one`,title:`Take key one from the Spikes`,text:`Light the two doorway torches using arrows through the central flame, or Din’s Fire. Enter and defeat the three Spikes when their spines retract. Open the chest for the first required Small Key.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-compass`,title:`Open the southern Compass route`,text:`Break the southern rock wall and sink along the passage. Defeat the Shell Blade by Hookshotting its open mouth. Surface, press the switch, Hookshot to the rising statue and clear the enemies beyond. Open the Compass chest.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-key-two`,title:`Take key two beyond the whirlpool`,text:`Return to the main room’s bottom east route and push the block into the water. Follow the passage to the whirlpool. Sink onto its submerged ledge, Hookshot the statue-mouth switch, remove the boots and dash through the timed gate. Surface for the second key.`,evidence:[`water-check`]},{id:`water-temple-middle`,title:`Raise the water halfway`,text:`Spend a key on the central pillar’s door. Hookshot to the inner ledge and play Zelda’s Lullaby at its crest. The water rises to the middle level. Leave through the door beside the floating block. The basement below it is optional.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-key-three`,title:`Ride the eastern water lift for key three`,text:`At middle water, explore east. Clear the cracked passage and Stingers, Hookshot upward, then operate the crystal-controlled water lift. Its upper chest holds the third required key. Return to the main chamber.`,evidence:[`water-check`]},{id:`water-temple-high`,title:`Reach the highest crest`,text:`Unlock the western middle-level door. Hit the crystal, defeat the descending Tektite, stand on the water platform and trigger the crystal again. Ride up, follow the passage and play Zelda’s Lullaby at the high crest.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-waterfall`,title:`Climb the moving waterfall platforms`,text:`Unlock the top-floor west door. Descend to the lowest platform and use the Hookshot targets on the moving platforms to climb the waterfall. Go through the door at the top.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-dragon-heads`,title:`Raise and lower the dragon statues`,text:`Shoot the crystal to raise the heads, then Hookshot the first. Lower them, Hookshot the wall target across the room and climb over the lowered head. Raise them again to reach the next head. Lower once more, stand on that head and raise it beneath your feet to reach the exit. Clear the enemies and cross to the next room.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-dark-link`,title:`Wait for Dark Link’s openings`,text:`Cross the misty room to its far door, then return toward the tree. Avoid attacking Dark Link’s raised shield. Dodge his three-swing sequence and counter after the final swing. Later, evade the jump and charged spin before countering. Collect the Longshot beyond him.`,evidence:[`water-check`]},{id:`water-temple-river`,title:`Leave through the underground river`,text:`Use an overhead Longshot target beyond the chest and drop into the river. Avoid the whirlpools. Near its end, shoot the eye and Longshot through the timed gate, then follow the southern exit back toward the main room. This route does not award a required key.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-key-four`,title:`Collect the fourth and final key`,text:`Lower the water at Ruto’s crest, then raise it halfway inside the central pillar. From the pillar’s north side, activate the eye and Longshot through the timed gate. Follow the waterfall target to the block, pull it out and work around it to push from the other side. Surface beyond it for key four.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-north-route`,title:`Use the bottom north passage`,text:`Sink to the bottom north passage. Longshot across the spikes and unlock the door. Cross the room with water currents and rolling boulders to its opposite door; the Iron Boots help you hold your position when appropriate.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-stone-switch`,title:`Hold down the submerged switch`,text:`In the Stinger room, bomb the two weak wall sections to access both sides of the block. Push and pull it around the opened passage until it drops onto the floor switch. The water rises, allowing you to reach the next door.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-boss-key`,title:`Reach the Boss Key`,text:`Press the next switch and cross the three temporary water platforms. Wait for the rolling boulder to pass, walk through the waterfall and enter the left opening. Clear the Shell Blade or pass it carefully, then open the Boss Key chest beyond the door.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-boss-door`,title:`Restore high water for Morpha`,text:`Return to the high crest and raise the water fully. Longshot to the northern target in the main room. Wear the Iron Boots on the final current-swept slope, wait for the blade traps to pass and enter with the Boss Key.`,evidence:[`water-guide`]},{id:`water-temple-fire-arrows`,title:`Shoot into the sunrise`,text:`After Morpha, take the heart and the blue warp for the Water Medallion. Lake Hylia refills. On the lakeside platform with the inscription, face the rising sun and shoot a normal arrow into it. Swim to the little island where the Fire Arrows land and collect them for Ganon's Castle.`,evidence:[`items-guide`]}],changes:[`Four Small Keys are required, rather than the original N64 route’s six.`,`The central-pillar basement and Ruto’s cracked-wall room now hold optional Skulltulas.`,`Dark Link and Morpha have expanded attacks.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`The key numbers here count pickups, not the number currently in your inventory.`,`Follow the map’s east/west directions; do not substitute the original N64 key checklist.`],sources:[{id:`water-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Water Temple Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-water-temple-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`water-check`,label:`G2A · four-key remake Water Temple route`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-water-temple-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`items-guide`,label:`RPG Site · verified remake item locations`,href:`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21671-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-minimalist-100-walkthrough-all-items-gold-skulltula-tokens-heart-pieces`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Dark Link · Morpha`,strategy:[`Against Dark Link, let the combination, jump or spin finish before countering. His raised shield punishes repeated direct attacks.`,`Against Morpha, wait for the nucleus-bearing tentacle to finish its slam, pull the core with the Longshot and strike.`,`Run around the perimeter during spinning attacks. Among decoy tentacles, track the real nucleus; wall targets help you cross the arena.`,`Later groups and walls of tentacles still contain only one real core. Keep targeting that core rather than attacking water.`]}},{slug:`bottom-of-the-well`,title:`Bottom of the Well`,subtitle:`The hands have learned a new trick.`,description:`Drain the well as a child and win the Lenses of Truth through the remake’s Dead Hand encounter.`,category:`story`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Forest, Fire and Water Temples complete`,`Song of Storms`,`Zelda’s Lullaby`,`Magic`],reward:`Nocturne of Shadow · Lenses of Truth`,steps:[{id:`bottom-of-the-well-nocturne`,title:`Witness Kakariko's shadow`,text:`Visit Kakariko as an adult after completing the Forest, Fire and Water Temples. Watch the scene in the village and learn the Nocturne of Shadow from Sheik. If you have not learned the Song of Storms, visit the windmill musician now and show him the Ocarina.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-child`,title:`Return as a child`,text:`Travel to the Temple of Time and place the Master Sword in its pedestal. Return to Kakariko's windmill as child Link and play the Song of Storms for the musician. The mechanism speeds up and drains the well outside.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-false-wall`,title:`Enter the hidden chamber`,text:`Climb down the dry well and crawl through the narrow opening. Descend the ladder, defeat the Skulltula and walk through the apparently solid wall behind it. The dungeon uses false walls and floors, so move deliberately.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-drain`,title:`Drain the inner channels`,text:`Follow the shallow channel around the outer edge of the main chamber, avoiding the suspicious center. At the far end, find the large stone face pouring water and play Zelda's Lullaby on its Triforce mark. The channels drain.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-pit`,title:`Descend to the new Dead Hand encounter`,text:`From the drained statue ledge, follow the exposed crawlspace. Clear the Skulltula and pass the door. The chest ahead hides an invisible floor pit: drop through it to reach the foggy encounter room.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-dead-hand`,title:`Break the limbs, then strike the face`,text:`Approach an emerging arm to bait its lunge; retreat and attack while it recovers. Destroy the limbs to expose Dead Hand’s body. Guard until its head lowers, strike the face, then repeat when the limbs return. If grabbed, press buttons to break free.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-lenses`,title:`Take the Lenses of Truth`,text:`Open the chest after the fight. Equip the Lenses of Truth; D-pad Up now toggles the effect. It reveals the hidden exit and ladder. Switch it off when you have understood the room, since it consumes magic.`,evidence:[`well-guide`]},{id:`bottom-of-the-well-return-adult`,title:`Prepare for the Shadow Temple`,text:`Retrace the crawlspace and entrance ladder to leave. Return to the Temple of Time and become adult Link. Refill magic, bring Din's Fire and play the Nocturne of Shadow to reach the high graveyard entrance.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]}],changes:[`Dead Hand’s emerging limbs are defeated before its main body appears.`,`The Lenses of Truth use an Equipment shortcut on D-pad Up.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`The Lens is the only well reward needed for this main-story route. Map, Compass, optional keys and tokens remain side exploration.`],sources:[{id:`well-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Bottom Well Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-bottom-well-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`shadow-temple`,title:`Shadow Temple`,subtitle:`See the path. Break the statue.`,description:`Recover the Hover Boots, sail the ancient boat and survive the remake’s Bongo Bongo.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Nocturne of Shadow`,`Lenses of Truth`,`Din’s Fire`,`Bow`,`Longshot`,`Iron Boots`,`Magic`],reward:`Hover Boots · Shadow Medallion`,steps:[{id:`shadow-temple-entrance`,title:`Reveal and light the entrance torches`,text:`Warp with the Nocturne of Shadow. Use the Lens to reveal the ring of torches, stand on the central platform and cast Din’s Fire. Inside, Longshot the first gap and walk through the false wall.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-vulture`,title:`Point at the true skull`,text:`Use the Lens around the vulture statue: only the true skull remains visible. Rotate the beak toward it to open the far gate. Before attempting the gap, explore the northwest false wall.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-boots`,title:`Win the Hover Boots`,text:`Use the Lens to follow the hidden doors through the western/northwestern route. In Dead Hand’s room, destroy its emerging limbs; Din’s Fire can clear them together. Strike the body’s lowered head until it falls, then take the Hover Boots. Return to the vulture room.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-first-key`,title:`Open the crystal-room route`,text:`Hover across the first gap. At the Beamos hub, take the northern false-wall route and collect the five crystals around the scythes for a Small Key. Return, bomb the eastern rock wall and unlock the descending path.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-guillotines`,title:`Cross the guillotines and platforms`,text:`Pass each rising blade, using Hover Boots around the fast guillotines where needed. Defeat the Stalfos with the boots off. Take the moving platforms toward the Beamos and collect the five crystals, including the ones on invisible and raised platforms.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-crushers`,title:`Support the falling spike traps`,text:`Reveal the stone block with the Lens and push it beneath the crushers, staying clear of the unprotected trap. Move it to the far end, climb onto the upper structure and ride a crusher upward. Open the southwest chest for the next key.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-hidden-platforms`,title:`Collect the hidden room’s crystals`,text:`Return to the invisible platform and reveal the moving platform beneath it. Ride to the locked route. Use the Lens to avoid the floor spikes, defeat the ReDeads and collect the five crystals, reaching the high ones with the Longshot.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-skull-key`,title:`Bomb the giant skull`,text:`The crystal door leads to a room with a rotating skull. Kill all the Keese so you can leave, climb up and drop a bomb into the skull’s opening. Collect its Small Key. Return and use the high Longshot target to reach the locked exit.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-fans`,title:`Use both kinds of boots`,text:`Wear the Iron Boots to walk against the fans. Longshot to the wooden beam above the gap when needed. At the far end, reveal the false side wall with the Lens. Switch to the Hover Boots and let the fan carry you through that opening.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-fan-key`,title:`Break the wall beyond the fans`,text:`Use the fan and Hover Boots to reach the false side opening. Defeat the ReDeads, avoid the blade traps and break the rock wall. Take the Small Key and unlock the onward door.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-boat`,title:`Sail the ancient boat`,text:`Move the block beneath the ladder and climb aboard. Play Zelda's Lullaby on the Triforce. Fight the Stalfos while the boat moves. As it reaches the end and starts sinking, jump to the bank on the left.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-maze-key`,title:`Find the key beyond the web`,text:`Burn the web beside the landing with fire. Use the Lens through the invisible-wall maze and defeat its Floormasters. In the southern room, defeat the invisible Floormaster and all its small hands for a Small Key.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-boss-key`,title:`Burn the closing walls`,text:`Use that key on the northern door off the maze. Ready Din’s Fire or Fire Arrows before entering. Burn the wooden spike walls as they close in, defeat the ReDead and take the Boss Key.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-bridge`,title:`Topple the bird statue`,text:`Return to the boat landing. Break the cracked rock at the bird statue’s base to drop it into a bridge. Cross and take the southern door. Use the Lens and Hover Boots to follow the platforms to Bongo Bongo.`,evidence:[`shadow-guide`]},{id:`shadow-temple-medallion`,title:`Awaken the Shadow Sage`,text:`Defeat Bongo Bongo, collect the Heart Container and use the blue warp. With the Shadow Medallion earned, your next destination is the Gerudo fortress in western Hyrule.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]}],changes:[`The entrance torches are visible through the Lenses of Truth.`,`Collection rooms use crystals; the final bridge comes from breaking the bird statue’s base.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`Switch between ordinary movement, Hover Boots and Iron Boots when each obstacle calls for them.`],sources:[{id:`shadow-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Shadow Temple Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-shadow-temple-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`boss-guide`,label:`G2A · remake boss mechanics`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-boss-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Bongo Bongo`,strategy:[`Use Hover Boots briefly against the drum bounce, then remove them for normal movement.`,`Avoid a hand’s slam and hit it when it stops glowing. Arrows can reach hands beyond sword range. Disable both hands.`,`Reveal the body with the Lens, shoot the exposed eye as it charges, and run in for sword strikes.`,`Later hands sweep, grab or punch. Interrupt vulnerable hands with arrows and repeat the eye opening.`]}},{slug:`gerudo-and-wasteland`,title:`Gerudo Fortress & the desert`,subtitle:`Four carpenters. One guide only truth can reveal.`,description:`Earn the Gerudo Pass, follow the desert guide and learn the Requiem of Spirit.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Epona or Longshot`,`Lenses of Truth`,`Magic`],reward:`Gerudo Pass · Requiem of Spirit`,steps:[{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-valley`,title:`Cross the broken bridge`,text:`Enter Gerudo Valley from western Hyrule Field. Jump the broken bridge on Epona, or Longshot the wood on the far side. Speak to the carpenter boss by the tent, then follow the path into Gerudo's Fortress.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-escape-cell`,title:`Escape if the guards capture you`,text:`Enter the fortress and avoid the patrols. If captured, use the Longshot escape route above the cell and return to the connected corridors and rooftops. Consult the fortress map as you search for the four carpenter cells.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-shiro`,title:`Free Shiro`,text:`Find Shiro’s cell and speak to him to trigger the guard fight. Defend, dodge her spin and counter after her attack. Take the dropped Small Key, unlock his cell and speak to him again so he leaves.`,evidence:[`fortress-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-saburo`,title:`Free Saburo`,text:`Use the stairs, rooftops and connected interior passages to reach Saburo’s cell. Defeat the swordswoman, collect the cell key and release him. Afterward, continue through the remaining connected sections rather than retracing a completed cell.`,evidence:[`fortress-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-ichiro`,title:`Free Ichiro`,text:`Find Ichiro in another cell hall. Speak to him, win the next swordswoman encounter, take the key and open his cell. The fortress map helps distinguish this hall from the cells already visited.`,evidence:[`fortress-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-jiro`,title:`Free Jiro`,text:`Locate the remaining captive, Jiro. Defeat the final guard encounter, collect the Small Key and release him. Check that all four carpenters have left their cells.`,evidence:[`fortress-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-pass`,title:`Accept the captain’s request`,text:`After the rescues, agree to investigate Nabooru’s disappearance. Accept the Gerudo Pass, which allows free movement among the Gerudo. Head to the desert gate and speak with its gatekeeper to open the way.`,evidence:[`fortress-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-flags`,title:`Follow the desert flag posts`,text:`Longshot over the quicksand, then follow the flags through the storm. Identify the next post before leaving the previous one behind. Reach the stone shelter and climb to its roof.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-phantom-guide`,title:`Follow the Phantom Guide`,text:`Read the shelter’s plaque and activate the Lens. Speak to the revealed Phantom Guide and accept its offer. Follow closely through the sharp turns, avoiding Leevers, until the marked route reaches the Desert Colossus.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`gerudo-and-wasteland-requiem`,title:`Learn the route across time`,text:`Approach the Spirit Temple. Sheik stops you and teaches the Requiem of Spirit. Warp to the Temple of Time, become a child and use the Requiem to return to the Colossus.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]}],changes:[`The Gerudo Pass accompanies the captain’s request to find Nabooru.`,`Sheik teaches Requiem on the approach to the temple.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`The fortress has several connected indoor and rooftop routes. This guide uses the remake map and captive names rather than unverified N64 left/right doorway directions.`],sources:[{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`fortress-guide`,label:`Zelda Central · remake Gerudo Fortress`,href:`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/walkthrough/gerudo-fortress/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`spirit-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Spirit Temple Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-spirit-temple-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}]},{slug:`spirit-temple`,title:`Spirit Temple`,subtitle:`One temple. Two ages.`,description:`Recover the Silver Gauntlets as a child, then return for the Mirror Shield and Twinrova.`,category:`story`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Requiem of Spirit`,`Child and adult access`,`Boomerang`,`Bombchus`,`Longshot`,`Hover Boots`,`Megaton Hammer`,`Lenses of Truth`],reward:`Silver Gauntlets · Mirror Shield · Spirit Medallion`,steps:[{id:`spirit-temple-nabooru`,title:`Child: make a promise to Nabooru`,text:`Enter as child Link. Speak to Nabooru by the left crawlspace, say you dislike Ganondorf and agree to help. Crawl through, defeat the Keese and Armos, then take the left door.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-child-bridge`,title:`Child: lower the bridge`,text:`Defeat the Stalfos, then curve the Boomerang around the barrier into the crystal. Cross the lowered bridge and clear the Green Bubbles. Continue through the small passage to Anubis.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-child-anubis`,title:`Child: guide Anubis into fire`,text:`Hit the eye switch on the northwest pillar. Move across the room so Anubis mirrors your movement into the fire on the opposite pillar. Take the opened route.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-child-key`,title:`Child: collect the first key`,text:`Defeat the Keese and Wallmaster, then gather the five crystals, including the raised ones. Cross the lowered barrier and use a burning Deku Stick to light the torches. Take the key, return to the starting room, crawl through the central opening and unlock its door.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-sunlight`,title:`Child: let the sunlight in`,text:`Shoot the spiders on the climbable wall and climb. Defeat the Lizalfos. Hit the crystal switch to get Bombchus, then send one up the wall toward the cracked patch where sunlight leaks in. Its explosion widens the opening and activates the sun emblem.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-statue`,title:`Child: cross the statue chamber`,text:`In the giant-statue room, push the nearby Armos off the ledge onto its floor switch. Climb the stairs and continue. Lighting the two torches on the room's lower floor earns the optional map; the climbable wall beside the dropped Armos returns you upstairs.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-sun-block`,title:`Child: move the sun into the beam`,text:`Clear the Beamos and gather the five crystals from the walls and central climb. Move the sun-marked block into the light to reveal the Small Key chest. Collect it and unlock the route to the Iron Knuckle.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-silver`,title:`Child: collect the Silver Gauntlets`,text:`Wake the Iron Knuckle. Bait an axe swing, backflip clear and punish its recovery with the sword; pillars it breaks can release hearts. After winning, leave through the rear door and open the outdoor chest. Watch Nabooru's scene. Return to the Temple of Time, become adult Link and warp back.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-adult-block`,title:`Adult: open the other wing`,text:`Push the giant block on the entrance's right side until it drops. Bomb the Beamos and Longshot the ceiling crystal. The left room offers a Compass after a Wolfos fight and Zelda's Lullaby. Take the right door for the required silver-rupee room.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-adult-key`,title:`Adult: collect the boulder-room rupees`,text:`Use the Hover Boots for the floating rupee and check the alcoves. Move the Time Block with the Song of Time to reach the remaining rupee. Collect all five, enter the opened door, defeat the Like Like and take its key. Return and unlock the central route.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-mirror-room`,title:`Adult: direct the light`,text:`Pass the flying pots and Like Like, then climb the brick wall. Use the Lens to locate the invisible Floormaster; defeat it and its small hands. Rotate the mirror until its light strikes the sun that opens the exit. Avoid continuing to the sun that releases a Wallmaster.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-hand-key`,title:`Adult: play in the statue’s hand`,text:`Longshot to the statue’s left wrist and play Zelda’s Lullaby on its marked hand. Use the northeast target to reach the hammer switch and open the lower shortcut. Then Longshot to the opposite wrist for the Small Key chest. Return to the southeast stairs.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-anubis`,title:`Adult: light the Anubis route`,text:`Unlock the upper route and clear the Beamos. In the three-Anubis room, play the Song of Time at the far symbol. Activate the fire switch and use the Time Block and corners to steer the enemies into flame. In the next room, bait the Armos onto the blue switch.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-mirror-shield`,title:`Adult: win the Mirror Shield`,text:`Take the opened southern door and defeat the second Iron Knuckle with baited swings and counters. Outside, press the switch to reveal the chest and take the Mirror Shield. Return to the sunlit room; reflect light onto its sun and collect the key beyond it.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-boss-key`,title:`Adult: secure the Boss Key`,text:`Return through the Anubis room and open its remaining locked door. Longshot high onto the moving climbing wall to pass it. Continue to the Triforce and play Zelda's Lullaby. In the next room, smash or bomb the false door hiding an eye switch, shoot the eye, Longshot to the new platform and step on its switch. Open the Boss Key chest.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-mirrors`,title:`Adult: connect the two light beams`,text:`Climb to the upper mirror route. Drop to the reachable switch and strike it to open the raised door. Clear the Bubbles, break the cracked wall and defeat the Dinolfos. Rotate both mirrors so light travels through the opening and bars to the chained platform.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-face`,title:`Adult: lower the platform`,text:`Stand on the chained platform and use the Mirror Shield to illuminate the sun switch. As the platform lowers into the statue chamber, hold the beam on the giant statue's face until it crumbles. Longshot to the opening, use the Boss Key and defeat the final Iron Knuckle. Continue through the passage to Twinrova.`,evidence:[`spirit-guide`]},{id:`spirit-temple-spirit`,title:`Receive the Spirit Medallion`,text:`Win both phases of Twinrova, take the Heart Container and enter the warp. With all five temple sages awakened, return to the Temple of Time for the final revelation and the Light Arrows.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]}],changes:[`The child sun-block puzzle awards its key through sunlight.`,`The adult Anubis route uses a Time Block and fire switch.`,`The upper mirror switch is reached directly; the N64 barred spin-attack instruction does not apply.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`Silver Gauntlets are for adult Link. Keep the child and adult halves separate when following the checklist.`],sources:[{id:`spirit-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Spirit Temple Dungeon`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-spirit-temple-dungeon-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`boss-guide`,label:`G2A · remake boss mechanics`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-boss-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Twinrova`,strategy:[`Reflect one sister’s elemental beam into the opposite sister with the Mirror Shield.`,`When fused, absorb three attacks of the same element; dodge the opposite element so it does not reset your charge. Cross and attack after the reflected blast stuns her.`,`Use the side platforms to keep hazards away from the centre. Dodge her later charge and watch the wand she actually fires, since she can change it at the last moment.`]}},{slug:`ganons-castle`,title:`Ganon’s Castle & the final battle`,subtitle:`Six barriers. Three final phases.`,description:`Break the sage barriers, climb the tower and follow the remake’s expanded escape and Ganon battle.`,category:`story`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`All six Medallions`,`Light Arrows`,`Fire Arrows`,`Mirror Shield`,`Lenses of Truth`,`All main dungeon equipment`,`Magic`,`An empty bottle`],reward:`Golden Gauntlets · the end of the main story`,steps:[{id:`ganons-castle-bridge`,title:`Cross the sages' bridge`,text:`Visit the Temple of Time after all five adult temples to receive the Light Arrows. Refill arrows, magic and bottles, then go where Hyrule Castle stood. Approach the broken staircase at the chasm: the sages create a rainbow bridge. Enter and pass the Beamos to the barrier chamber.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-shadow-gauntlets`,title:`Shadow trial: obtain the Golden Gauntlets`,text:`Take the purple-marked door first. Longshot to the chest, then light the torch with a Fire Arrow to reveal temporary platforms. Cross with the Hover Boots. Use the Lens for the hidden path, reach the lower floor switch and press it. Longshot to the large chest it creates and take the Golden Gauntlets.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-shadow-clear`,title:`Shadow: lift the great rock`,text:`Use the Golden Gauntlets to throw the giant rock beside the chest. Follow the revealed path and press the switch. Use the Lens and Hover Boots across the hidden platforms. Shoot the barrier core beyond the door with a Light Arrow.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-forest`,title:`Forest: create the first foothold`,text:`Defeat the Wolfos and light all five torches. In the fan chamber, play the Song of Time by the left-hand symbol. Collect its crystal, then use Hover Boots, the floor switch and its Longshot target to gather the remaining four. Destroy the barrier with a Light Arrow.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-water`,title:`Water trial: solve the ice blocks`,text:`Defeat the Freezards, bottle blue fire, melt the red ice and refill before leaving. In the timed block room, push the far block into the hole. Use it as a stopper for the remaining block: slide that block toward the filled hole, then toward the back and across beneath the high red-ice ledge. Climb, melt the ice, hammer the switch and destroy the blue orb.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-fire`,title:`Fire: make a crossing from the stalactite`,text:`Throw aside the giant entrance rock and equip the Goron Tunic. Gather the five crystals before the platforms sink. Throw the internal giant rock into the hanging stalactite to make the remaining crossing. Longshot to the exit and destroy the red barrier core.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-light`,title:`Light: find the invisible key`,text:`Defeat the invisible enemies. In the following Triforce room, use the Lens to find the invisible key chest; the Lullaby chest only contains a rupee. Unlock the route, gather five crystals around the rolling boulders and ceiling target, then pass the false wall and destroy the real core.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-spirit`,title:`Spirit: send a Bombchu over the fence`,text:`Gather the five crystals around the blade traps, moving statues when needed. Clear the Torch Slugs and send a Bombchu over the mesh wall into the distant switch. Burn the ceiling web; reflect sunlight into the green-filling sun to the right of the doorway you entered. Destroy the final core.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-refill`,title:`Refill before entering the tower`,text:`Use the Lens beneath the central bridge to find the hidden fairy room. The optional Great Fairy outside is behind a giant rock and offers halved damage for 500 Rupees. Refill arrows and magic, then enter the cleared central tower.`,evidence:[`route-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-tower`,title:`Take the Boss Key after the Iron Knuckles`,text:`Defeat the Dinolfos, then both Stalfos. Continue to the two Iron Knuckles; begin with one, but expect the second to wake as the first loses its armour. Defeat both and open the Boss Key chest. Climb onward and unlock Ganondorf’s door.`,evidence:[`final-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-ganondorf`,title:`Return the volley, then fire a Light Arrow`,text:`Manually aim during this fight. Return Ganondorf’s energy sphere with timed sword swings. When it hits him, shoot a Light Arrow and cross to strike. Retreat before the next exchange; expect faster volleys and disappearing floor. Use climbable walls if you fall.`,evidence:[`boss-guide`,`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-escape-stalfos`,title:`Follow Zelda through the first gates`,text:`Follow Zelda down the collapsing tower and wait for her to unlock each gate. Defeat the two Stalfos in the sealed room, then continue to the broken bridge. Longshot its far target to cross with Zelda.`,evidence:[`final-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-escape-rubble`,title:`Break the rubble while Zelda holds the enemies`,text:`After the floor collapses, Zelda holds the enemies back. Smash the blocking rubble with the Megaton Hammer and follow the exit. When she freezes the ReDeads ahead, clear the path and continue through the last gate.`,evidence:[`final-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-ganon-tail`,title:`Ganon: break the tail crystal`,text:`Without the Master Sword, evade Ganon’s swings and wait for a heavy blade to stick in the ground. Move behind him and strike the glowing tail crystal with your available weapon, such as the Megaton Hammer. Break it to advance; Zelda returns the Master Sword.`,evidence:[`final-guide`,`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-ganon-supplies`,title:`Recover supplies from the ruined walls`,text:`If hearts, arrows or magic run low, bait Ganon’s blades into the ruined walls around the arena. Collect the released supplies when there is a safe opening.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-ganon-arms`,title:`Ganon: destroy both glowing arms`,text:`Equip the Master Sword. Avoid the marked lightning strikes. Attack a glowing arm when his blade is stuck, or hit it with Light Arrows from a safe opening. Break both arms, then keep moving around the arena during his charge until Zelda opens his forehead eye.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]},{id:`ganons-castle-ganon-eye`,title:`Ganon: expose the final opening`,text:`Dodge the ground ruptures and shoot the open forehead eye with Light Arrows. After three hits he falls. Approach and strike with the Master Sword to finish the battle, then watch the sages seal him away.`,evidence:[`castle-guide`]}],changes:[`The Light trial’s required key is in an invisible chest; its Lullaby chest has a rupee.`,`The tower Boss Key appears after the Iron Knuckles.`,`Zelda returns the Master Sword; Ganon then exposes his arms and forehead eye.`],notes:[`Edition-specific guides checked on 5 November 2026. This is documentary verification; HyruleAtlas has not replayed these steps on a Switch 2 console.`,`This finishes the main story. It does not certify every optional Heart Piece, Skulltula or side quest.`,`Golden Gauntlets open the Fire and Light trial entrances; the other trials can be entered earlier.`],sources:[{id:`castle-guide`,label:`Polygon · Johnny Yu · Ganondorfs Castle`,href:`https://www.polygon.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-oot-ganondorfs-castle-walkthrough/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`route-guide`,label:`Respec · tested Switch 2 route`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`final-guide`,label:`Zelda Central · remake Ganondorf and Ganon`,href:`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/walkthrough/ganondorf-and-ganon/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`boss-guide`,label:`G2A · remake boss mechanics`,href:`https://www.g2a.com/news/features/guide/ocarina-of-time-remake-boss-guide/`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}],boss:{name:`Ganondorf → Ganon`,strategy:[`Ganondorf: win the energy volley, shoot the exposed chest with a Light Arrow, then use the sword.`,`Ganon begins with the tail crystal. After Zelda returns the Master Sword, attack the glowing arms and avoid lightning.`,`After both arms break, evade his charge. Zelda opens the forehead eye: use Light Arrows, then the Master Sword for the ending.`]}}],n=`2026-11-05`,r=[{id:`rpg-route`,label:`RPG Site — Switch 2 item route`,href:`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21671-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-minimalist-100-walkthrough-all-items-gold-skulltula-tokens-heart-pieces`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:n,edition:`switch2-remake`},{id:`respec-route`,label:`Respec — remake walkthrough`,href:`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:n,edition:`switch2-remake`}];function i(e,t,n){return[...t].sort((e,t)=>e[1].localeCompare(t[1],`en`)||e[2].localeCompare(t[2],`en`)).map(([t,r,i,a,o])=>({id:`${e}-${String(t).padStart(3,`0`)}`,title:`${r} — ${i}`,text:a,evidence:[...o??[n]]}))}var a=[[1,`Great Deku Tree`,`Compass-room alcove`,`Child route: raise the Compass-room platforms, enter the side alcove and defeat the Gold Skulltula inside.`],[2,`Great Deku Tree`,`Basement climbing vines`,`Child route: after reaching the basement, inspect the vines leading back upward; climb to recover the token.`],[3,`Great Deku Tree`,`Northern basement grate`,`Child route: search the northern grate in the large basement chamber, separate from the spider on the climbing vines.`],[4,`Great Deku Tree`,`Torch-room web`,`Child route: burn the web concealing the optional area beside the torch puzzle, then search beyond it.`],[5,`Castle Town`,`Pot-room moving crate`,`Child route: enter the pot-filled room near the town entrance and break the visibly moving crate to expose the spider.`],[6,`Lon Lon Ranch`,`Tree behind the Cucco building`,`Child route: circle behind the Super Cucco minigame building and roll into the tree to dislodge the spider.`],[7,`Kakariko Village`,`Watchtower ladder`,`Child route, night: examine the watchtower ladder and collect the token from the Gold Skulltula attached to it.`],[8,`Kakariko Village`,`House of Skulltula doorway`,`Child route, night: inspect the wall beside the cursed family's front door, rather than searching inside their house.`],[9,`Kakariko Village`,`Construction site`,`Child route, night: search the unfinished building in the middle of the village for this outdoor Gold Skulltula.`],[10,`Kakariko Village`,`Village-centre tree`,`Child route, night: roll into the central village tree, then defeat the spider that falls from its branches.`],[11,`Kakariko Village`,`Northwestern house`,`Child route, night: walk around the northwestern house and check its rear wall for a separate village token.`],[12,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Northwestern soil patch`,`Child route: release a bottled bug into the soft soil in the graveyard's northwest corner; defeat the emerging spider.`],[13,`Kokiri Forest`,`Know-It-All Brothers' house`,`Child route, night: go behind the southwestern house occupied by the Know-It-All Brothers and search its exterior wall.`],[14,`Lost Woods`,`Two-left-turn soil patch`,`Child route: take the left branch from Kokiri Forest, then the next left; release a bug into the soil.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[15,`Death Mountain Trail`,`Dodongo entrance soil`,`Child route: after opening Dodongo Cavern, release a bottled bug into the soil patch directly outside its entrance.`],[16,`Dodongo Cavern`,`Rear of the bomb staircase`,`Child route: raise the staircase with the ring of Bomb Flowers; circle behind its upper section and look upward.`],[17,`Dodongo Cavern`,`Shortcut-platform side chamber`,`Child route, Bomb Bag: beside the new central-chamber shortcut, bomb the cracked rock on the right and search the room.`],[18,`Dodongo Cavern`,`Baby Dodongo corridor wall`,`Child route, Bomb Bag: revisit the southeastern first-floor Baby Dodongo corridor and bomb its cracked side wall.`],[19,`Dodongo Cavern`,`Skull-mouth block puzzle`,`Child route: inside the giant skull's mouth, bomb the optional cracked wall along the block-pushing route.`],[20,`Death Mountain Trail`,`Wall above Kakariko`,`Child route, Bomb Bag: on the descent toward Kakariko, open the cracked wall and collect the token behind it.`],[21,`Goron City`,`Western treasure room`,`Child route, Bomb Bag: clear the western room's bombable rocks; search beyond the rupee chests for the spider.`],[22,`Death Mountain Crater`,`Summit-entrance crates`,`Child route: enter beside the summit Fairy Fountain, turn left and break the crates; leave before the heat timer expires.`],[23,`Zora River`,`Bean-seller soil`,`Child route: beside the Magic Bean seller, empty a bottled bug onto the soft soil and collect the emerging token.`],[24,`Zora River`,`Rocks below the waterfall plinth`,`Child route: descend carefully below the Triforce plinth near the waterfall and inspect the backs of the rock formations.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[25,`Lake Hylia`,`Laboratory soil`,`Child route: release a bottled bug into the soft soil outside the Lakeside Laboratory; keep this separate from its wall token.`],[26,`Zora Fountain`,`Tree near Jabu-Jabu`,`Child route: roll into the tree in the fountain area to reveal the spider hidden above ground.`],[27,`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,`Vines opposite the Map`,`Child route: in the Dungeon Map area, raise the water and inspect the climbable vines opposite the chest.`],[28,`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,`New hole after the tentacles`,`Child route, Boomerang: defeat the tentacles, drop through the newly accessible hole and check the landing area immediately.`],[29,`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,`Ceiling beyond the tentacle drop`,`Child route, Boomerang: after the tentacle-drop token, follow the exit passage and aim at the spider on the ceiling.`],[30,`Jabu-Jabu's Belly`,`Final vines before Barinade`,`Child route, Boomerang: in the last room before the boss, look up at the vines and retrieve their token.`],[31,`Zora Fountain`,`Wall beside Jabu-Jabu`,`Child route, night: return with the Boomerang and check the wall to Jabu-Jabu's right for the high spider.`],[32,`Lake Hylia`,`Laboratory bridge-side wall`,`Child route, night: stand on the laboratory bridge and use the Boomerang to recover the token from its exterior wall.`],[33,`Lake Hylia`,`Southwestern crawlspace`,`Child route: reach the small land outcrop at the lake's far southwest and crawl through its narrow opening.`],[34,`Lon Lon Ranch`,`Ranch window`,`Child route, night: use the Boomerang on the spider attached to the ranch building's window.`],[35,`Lon Lon Ranch`,`Southwestern ruined building`,`Child route, night: revisit the ruined building used for the block-puzzle fragment; recover its exterior token with the Boomerang.`],[36,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Behind Dampé's hut`,`Child route, night: search behind Dampé's hut and use the Boomerang to bring the token within reach.`],[37,`Hyrule Field`,`Tree at the forest-side stream`,`Child route, night: follow the stream near the Kokiri approach to its lone tree; roll into the trunk.`],[38,`Kokiri Forest`,`Shop soil`,`Child route: release a bottled bug into the soft soil behind the shop, then defeat the spider it flushes out.`],[39,`Lost Woods`,`Forest Stage soil`,`Child route: reach the Forest Stage clearing, then release a bug into its soft soil before planting a bean.`],[40,`Gerudo Valley`,`Small entrance bridge`,`Child route, night: inspect underneath the small plank bridge near the valley entrance before reaching the large suspension bridge.`],[41,`Gerudo Valley`,`Cow-ledge soil`,`Child route: use the Cucco to reach the lower ledge with a cow and Gerudo; release a bug into its soil.`],[42,`Kakariko Village`,`Behind the southern rooftop`,`Adult route, night: Hookshot to the southern house's vines, climb onto its roof and check behind it.`],[43,`Kokiri Forest`,`Southeastern house`,`Adult route, night: search behind the southeastern house and use the Hookshot to recover the wall token.`],[44,`Lost Woods`,`Forest Stage bean ride`,`Adult route: pass Mido, turn left toward the Forest Stage clearing and ride the bean planted there as a child.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[45,`Sacred Forest Meadow`,`Maze right-hand wall`,`Adult route: halfway through the maze, inspect the high wall on the right and use the Hookshot.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[46,`Forest Temple`,`Entrance vines`,`Adult route: climb the first room's vines and search the upper section with the Hookshot before entering the lobby.`],[47,`Forest Temple`,`Northern lobby doorway`,`Adult route: stand at the lobby's northern door, face back into the room and inspect the wall to your left.`],[48,`Forest Temple`,`Balcony after the Boss Key`,`Adult route: drop through the Boss Key room's hole, exit onto the balcony and follow its ledge south.`],[49,`Forest Temple`,`Scarecrow above the shortcut`,`Adult route: after pushing the shortcut block down, look above the doorway; summon Pierre and Hookshot onto the high ledge.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[50,`Forest Temple`,`Rotating basement alcove`,`Adult route: while rotating the basement chamber toward the boss, inspect the side alcoves exposed by each position.`],[51,`Dodongo Cavern`,`Scarecrow in Baby Dodongo corridor`,`Adult route: revisit the lower eastern Baby Dodongo corridor, play the Scarecrow's Song and Hookshot toward Pierre.`],[52,`Goron City`,`Back of the central rock`,`Adult route: circle the rock where the bridges meet, then descend toward its rear climbing grate to reach the spider.`,[`rpg-route`,`respec-route`]],[53,`Fire Temple`,`Rising lava platform`,`Adult route: in the lava-platform room, ride the rising northwestern platform and use the Song of Time to open access.`],[54,`Fire Temple`,`Boulder-maze cracked wall`,`Adult route, Bomb Bag: inspect the large rolling-boulder maze's cracked wall and blast it open for the hidden spider.`],[55,`Fire Temple`,`Scarecrow elevator room`,`Adult route: from the upper boulder-maze area, face southwest, summon Pierre and ride the elevator to the hidden room.`],[56,`Fire Temple`,`Room beyond the Scarecrow elevator`,`Adult route: continue through the door from the Scarecrow elevator room; check immediately around the corner for the second spider.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[57,`Fire Temple`,`Hammer-route stones`,`Adult route, Megaton Hammer: reopen the first room's right-hand route and smash the stones near the end of its northern room.`],[58,`Death Mountain Trail`,`Rocks on the summit climb`,`Adult route, Megaton Hammer: descend the stretch that suffered falling rocks in childhood and break the obstructing hammer rocks.`],[59,`Death Mountain Trail`,`Rock near Goron City's gate`,`Adult route, Megaton Hammer: smash the rock near Goron City's entrance and the old Bomb Flower throwing point.`],[60,`Death Mountain Crater`,`Warp-point soil`,`Child route, Bolero of Fire: warp into the crater and release a bug into the soft soil near the landing point.`],[61,`Zora River`,`Western high ledge`,`Adult route, night: ride the childhood bean to the Gossip Stone ledge; search its western end with the Hookshot.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[62,`Zora River`,`High eastern wall`,`Adult route, night: near the river's final eastern bend, turn back and aim high on the wall with the Hookshot.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[63,`Zora Domain`,`Diving-game ledge`,`Adult route: stand where the childhood diving minigame started, look left and Hookshot the spider above the frozen domain.`],[64,`Ice Cavern`,`Spinning-blade chamber`,`Adult route: in the first spinning-blade room, look high above the floor and retrieve the token with the Hookshot.`],[65,`Ice Cavern`,`Compass-room northwest wall`,`Adult route: stand beside the Compass chest and look upward to the northwest; this token is separate from the removed fragment.`],[66,`Ice Cavern`,`Ice-block room entrance`,`Adult route: step onto the sliding-block room's icy floor, turn back toward the doorway and aim high with the Hookshot.`],[67,`Water Temple`,`Passage under the floating block`,`Adult route, green water level: sink inside the central pillar, pass beneath the raised block and open the B1F side room.`],[68,`Water Temple`,`Whirlpool passage`,`Adult route, Longshot: after obtaining the upgrade, inspect the wall above the whirlpool passage's water while following the exit.`],[69,`Water Temple`,`Central pillar's upper interior`,`Adult route, Longshot: return to the central pillar at the green water level and grapple to its high ceiling target.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[70,`Water Temple`,`Waterfall by the Boss Key route`,`Adult route: after collecting the Boss Key, return to the rolling-boulder corridor and inspect the wall above the cascading water.`],[71,`Water Temple`,`Blue route's green-level wall`,`Adult route, green water level: surface along the blue-lit water-lowering route; bomb the exposed cracked wall and search inside.`],[72,`Lake Hylia`,`Tree after the Water Temple`,`Adult route, Longshot: near the post-temple landing point, grapple to the tree's vines and climb up to the spider.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[73,`Lake Hylia`,`Laboratory tank bottom`,`Adult route, Iron Boots: sink inside the laboratory tank and collect the token with the Hookshot, which works underwater.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[74,`Hyrule Castle`,`Tree beside the climbing vine`,`Child route, night: inside the castle grounds, inspect the tree behind the wall beside the entrance climbing vine; roll into it.`],[75,`Hyrule Castle`,`Storms grotto near Talon's spot`,`Child route, Song of Storms: near Talon's former sleeping place, play beside the corner tree to uncover the token's grotto.`],[76,`Bottom of the Well`,`Room beyond the Beamos`,`Child route, Lenses of Truth: reveal the safe floor around the Beamos and enter the opposite room to find the spider.`],[77,`Bottom of the Well`,`Western locked room`,`Child route, small key: unlock the central area's western door, defeat the Deku Baba and collect the token.`],[78,`Bottom of the Well`,`Eastern hidden route`,`Child route, Lenses of Truth: explore the central area's eastern rooms and reveal the concealed route to the spider.`],[79,`Shadow Temple`,`Like Like side room`,`Adult route: in the invisible-scythe area, defeat the Like Like and enter the unlocked room containing the token and two chests.`],[80,`Shadow Temple`,`Top of the falling spikes`,`Adult route: use the movable block as protection, then climb above the spike traps and inspect the upper left side.`],[81,`Shadow Temple`,`Fan-gap rear wall`,`Adult route: after Hookshotting across the gap in front of a fan, turn around before continuing through the wind corridor.`],[82,`Shadow Temple`,`Scarecrow above the boat shortcut`,`Adult route: beside the boat-area shortcut block, summon Pierre above its enclosure and Hookshot up to the token.`],[83,`Shadow Temple`,`Three skull pots`,`Adult route, Bomb Bag: enter the room containing three skull-shaped pots and throw bombs into each to expose the token.`],[84,`Gerudo Valley`,`Tent-side rock formation`,`Adult route, night: search the rocky formation near the carpenter tents for a token separate from the one behind the tents.`],[85,`Gerudo Valley`,`Behind the carpenter tents`,`Adult route, night: walk around the rear of the carpenter tents and inspect the wall before leaving the valley.`],[86,`Gerudo Fortress`,`Eastern exterior wall`,`Adult route: inspect the fortress's eastern outside wall; collecting it is easier once the carpenters' rescue allows free movement.`],[87,`Gerudo Fortress`,`Rear of the archery target`,`Adult route, night: enter the Horseback Archery area and search behind the northeastern target, away from its shooting face.`],[88,`Mirage Desert`,`Guide-building basement`,`Adult route: reach the building along the flag trail, descend through its central opening and search the basement.`],[89,`Desert Colossus`,`Rocks beneath the birds`,`Adult route, night: inspect the northern rocky area beneath circling birds before entering the Spirit Temple.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[90,`Desert Colossus`,`Temple-entrance soil`,`Child route, Requiem of Spirit: release a bug into the soil left of the Spirit Temple entrance before planting a bean.`],[91,`Spirit Temple`,`Child silver-rupee gate`,`Child route: after collecting the five silver rupees to open the gate, inspect the area immediately beyond it.`],[92,`Spirit Temple`,`Right of the great statue`,`Child route: at the Dungeon Map chest beneath the great statue, look toward the statue's far right side.`],[93,`Spirit Temple`,`Door after the sunlight blocks`,`Child route: leave the sunlight-and-block puzzle room, then turn around and look above the doorway you just used.`],[94,`Desert Colossus`,`Bean-ride rock`,`Adult route, night: ride the bean planted beside the temple entrance and jump onto the rock carrying the spider.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]],[95,`Spirit Temple`,`Song of Time alcove`,`Adult route: in the rolling-boulder silver-rupee room, move the blue block with the Song of Time and check both alcoves.`],[96,`Spirit Temple`,`Scarecrow beside the statue's hand`,`Adult route: from the great statue's chest-bearing hand, reach the nearby ledge, summon Pierre and Hookshot to the high token.`],[97,`Castle Town Ruins`,`Collapsed building near the castle`,`Adult route, after Light Arrows: before entering Ganondorf's castle, inspect the rear of the collapsed building outside.`],[98,`Hyrule Field`,`Western marsh grotto`,`Late-adventure route: locate the grotto in the western marshland and break its crate to expose the Gold Skulltula.`],[99,`Hyrule Field`,`Southern woodland fissure`,`Late-adventure route, Bomb Bag: blast the ground crack in the woodland between Lon Lon Ranch and Lake Hylia; enter the grotto.`],[100,`Zora Fountain`,`Gauntlet-rock cave`,`Adult route, Silver Gauntlets: lift the rock beside the Fairy Fountain and follow the invisible-enemy cave to the upper token.`,[`rpg-tokens`,`respec-route`]]],o=[[1,`Lon Lon Ranch`,`Ruined-building crawlspace`,`Child route: enter the southwestern ruined building, rearrange its blocks and crawl through the opening to the fragment.`],[2,`Kakariko Village`,`Blue-roofed house resident`,`Child route: use the Cucco above the windmill to glide onto the blue-roofed house, then speak to its rooftop resident.`],[3,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Dampé's digging prize`,`Child route, night: join Dampé's digging tour; when he reports something hard, pay for the extra digging to uncover the fragment.`],[4,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Moveable gravestone`,`Child route, night: pull back the gravestones and inspect the hidden chamber containing the fragment; the remake changes this old reward route.`],[5,`Lost Woods`,`Two Skull Kids' music game`,`Child route, ocarina: stand on the stump facing the two musical Skull Kids and complete their repeated-note challenges.`],[6,`Lost Woods`,`Lone Skull Kid`,`Child route: take the first left from Kokiri Forest and play Saria's Song for the lone Skull Kid.`],[7,`Goron City`,`Spinning central pot`,`Child route: light the surrounding torches to activate the large pot, then land a bomb inside for its fragment prize.`],[8,`Kakariko Village`,`Roof below the owl landing`,`Child route: accept the owl's flight from Death Mountain, then descend from his landing roof toward the lower roof to the south.`],[9,`Castle Town`,`Bombchu Bowling prize`,`Child route, Bomb Bag: visit Bombchu Bowling and win its heart-fragment prize; the remake's entry fee is 10 rupees.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[10,`Castle Town`,`Richard's owner`,`Child route, night: speak to a white dog so it follows you, then bring it to Richard's owner until she recognises hers.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[11,`Zora River`,`High Cucco ledge`,`Child route: carry the entrance Cucco to the climbing vines; obtain the Cucco above them and glide to the isolated fragment.`],[12,`Zora River`,`Waterfall-side ledge`,`Child route: keep a Cucco while climbing toward the waterfall and glide onto the nearby ledge holding this separate fragment.`],[13,`Zora Domain`,`Torch challenge chest`,`Child route: light the domain's torches quickly with fire and a Deku Stick, then open the chest behind the waterfall.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[14,`Lake Hylia`,`Child fishing prize`,`Child route: catch a fish at least 55 centimetres long at the Fishing Pond and show it to the proprietor.`],[15,`Gerudo Valley`,`Ledge left of the large bridge`,`Child route: take the valley Cucco and glide southwest from the suspension bridge toward the lower ledge with a chest.`],[16,`Gerudo Valley`,`Behind the waterfall`,`Child route: reach the lower riverbank ledge with the Cucco, then follow the northern path and stairs behind the waterfall.`],[17,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Bean-ride ledge`,`Adult route: ride the bean planted in the graveyard as a child to reach the ledge holding the fragment.`],[18,`Kakariko Village`,`Windmill upper ledge`,`Adult route: finish Dampé's Hookshot challenge, follow its exit into the windmill and collect the fragment from the upper ledge.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[19,`Kakariko Graveyard`,`Dampé's faster race`,`Adult route: repeat Dampé's race after obtaining the Hookshot and finish in under one minute for the fragment.`],[20,`Lake Hylia`,`Laboratory roof`,`Adult route: ride the bean planted outside the laboratory as a child, dismount onto the roof and climb to the fragment.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[21,`Death Mountain Trail`,`Above Dodongo Cavern`,`Adult route: ride the bean planted beside Dodongo Cavern's entrance as a child to reach the fragment above the cave.`],[22,`Death Mountain Crater`,`Southern climbing grates`,`Adult route: descend carefully beside the two climbing grates in the crater's southern section to reach the lower fragment ledge.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[23,`Kakariko Village`,`Fifty-token reward`,`Either-age route: bring the cursed family fifty Gold Skulltula tokens and speak to their father to receive the fragment.`],[24,`Death Mountain Crater`,`Warp-point bean ride`,`Adult route: plant a bean beside the crater warp point as a child, return as an adult and ride the plant.`],[25,`Zora Fountain`,`Eastern ice-block route`,`Adult route: cross the detached floating ice blocks toward the eastern ledge and pick up the visible fragment.`],[26,`Zora Fountain`,`Underwater fragment`,`Adult route, Iron Boots: sink into the fountain near the Ice Cavern approach, collect the bottom fragment and return to air.`],[27,`Lake Hylia`,`Scientist's diving test`,`Adult route, Golden Scale: touch the laboratory tank's bottom by diving without Iron Boots, then speak to the scientist.`],[28,`Zora River`,`Frogs' storm song`,`Child route: stand before the frogs halfway along the river and play the Song of Storms for their first fragment.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[29,`Zora River`,`Frogs' butterfly game`,`Child route: grow all five frogs by playing their songs, then complete the butterfly-and-button minigame for a second fragment.`,[`rpg-route`,`respec-route`]],[30,`Castle Town`,`Treasure Chest Shop`,`Child route, night: complete the Treasure Chest Shop's chest sequence; use the Lenses of Truth to identify the winning choices.`],[31,`Gerudo Fortress`,`Highest rooftop chest`,`Adult route, Hookshot: climb above the prison area, find the high rooftop chest and grapple across to open it.`],[32,`Gerudo Fortress`,`Thousand-point archery prize`,`Adult route, Epona and bow: enter Horseback Archery during the day and score at least 1,000 points for the fragment.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[33,`Desert Colossus`,`Bean-ride upper rock`,`Adult route: ride the bean planted beside the Spirit Temple as a child, continuing past the token rock to the fragment.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`respec-route`]],[34,`Hyrule Field`,`Time-locked canyon chest`,`Read the fairy thought beside the empty chest as an adult; return as a child and open it for the fragment.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`rpg-route`,`respec-route`]],[35,`Hyrule Field`,`Password grotto near Castle Town`,`Read the lone-tree fairy thought as an adult; as a child, give the grotto's Business Scrub its password and pay 100 rupees.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`rpg-route`,`respec-route`]],[36,`Death Mountain Crater`,`Business Scrub below the summit`,`Child route, 100 rupees: enter from the summit, descend left to the Business Scrub and buy the fragment before overheating.`,[`rpg-fragments`,`rpg-route`,`respec-route`]]],s=[{slug:`gold-skulltulas`,title:`All 100 Gold Skulltula tokens`,subtitle:`A regional checklist for the Switch 2 remake`,description:`Find the token matching your current region, era and equipment. These edition-specific documentary records keep collection checks separate from the main-story route.`,category:`collection`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Use the era and equipment stated on each entry; not every token is available on the first visit.`,`For soil entries, carry a bug in a bottle; Magic Beans serve different later routes.`,`Several high tokens need the Boomerang, Hookshot or Longshot; Scarecrow routes also need the song prepared across both ages.`],reward:`100 recorded token locations; milestone rewards are claimed from the cursed family in Kakariko.`,steps:i(`gs`,a,`rpg-tokens`),changes:[`The remake's map records regional discoveries and can show the locations already found; launch reporting describes fuller regional totals after the ending.`,`The Echo Gem is the remake's nearby-Skulltula aid. Equip it when retracing a region.`,`Goron City's central-rock token is a separate adult revisit; include it when returning to the city.`],notes:[`A check means you marked this token collected. It does not read or synchronise the console save.`,`These locations were checked against documentary guides explicitly covering the 2026 Switch 2 remake. We have not personally tested all 100 on a console.`,`RPG Site and Respec are related publications; matching their routes is a documentary cross-check, not independent playtesting.`,`Entries are grouped by region. Their gs identifiers are stable HyruleAtlas checklist identifiers, not official map numbers.`,`The tree above Lake Hylia and the laboratory tank each contain a separate token; collecting one does not replace the other.`,`Time is stated where the inspected sources specify it. If an outdoor spider is absent, revisit at night and compare the game's regional counter.`,`This token checklist does not certify completion of the Hall of Fallen Foes, fairy thoughts or ZELDA NOTES.`],sources:[{id:`rpg-tokens`,label:`RPG Site — remake Gold Skulltula locations`,href:`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21634-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-gold-skulltula-locations-guide`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:n,edition:`switch2-remake`},...r]},{slug:`heart-pieces`,title:`All 36 Pieces of Heart`,subtitle:`Every fragment, region by region`,description:`Track each heart fragment by region. The remake adds time-travel clues and relocates rewards, so this list preserves the required era and access conditions.`,category:`collection`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Check the era, minigame result and inventory named on each entry before travelling.`,`Plant the relevant Magic Bean as a child before taking an adult bean route.`,`The two Hyrule Field fairy-thought rewards require an adult discovery followed by a childhood return.`],reward:`36 heart fragments recorded individually. Four fragments form one heart container; boss containers are a separate reward category.`,steps:i(`hp`,o,`rpg-fragments`),changes:[`Do not search the original Ice Cavern heart-fragment spot: the remake's late collection route instead includes a child Business Scrub in Death Mountain Crater.`,`Two Hyrule Field rewards depend on first reading their fairy thought as an adult; visiting the child location alone is insufficient.`,`For the frogs' second fragment, growing them is preparation: the butterfly minigame must also be completed.`],notes:[`These are edition-specific documentary instructions, not a claim that we personally collected every fragment on a console.`,`The 36-fragment total does not mean 36 full hearts or establish a verified maximum-health HUD.`,`The highest-roof chest, bean routes and two-era clues are listed separately even when they share a region.`,`For the password grotto, reports differ on left/right descriptions of the castle approach. Use the single-tree strip and its fairy thought rather than an unsupported compass direction.`,`RPG Site and Respec share editorial provenance; agreement between them is not independent gameplay evidence.`,`After the ending, compare the game's regional collection counters before concluding a missing fragment is elsewhere.`,`Stable hp identifiers belong to this checklist; they are not an official collection order.`],sources:[{id:`rpg-fragments`,label:`RPG Site — remake heart-fragment locations`,href:`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21635-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-heart-piece-locations-guide`,basis:`edition-guide`,publishedOn:`2026-11-05`,checkedOn:n,edition:`switch2-remake`},...r]}],c=(e,t,n,r=`edition-guide`,i=`2026-11-05`)=>({id:e,label:t,href:n,basis:r,...i?{publishedOn:i}:{},checkedOn:`2026-11-05`,edition:`switch2-remake`}),l=c(`respec`,`Respec · Alex Donaldson · tested remake route`,`https://www.respec.net/guide/276-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-walkthrough-100-completion-guide-with-all-switch-2-changes`,`firsthand-guide`),u=c(`rpgsite`,`RPG Site · remake completion route`,`https://www.rpgsite.net/guide/21671-the-legend-zelda-ocarina-time-remake-minimalist-100-walkthrough-all-items-gold-skulltula-tokens-heart-pieces`),d=c(`bottles`,`Shacknews · all five bottles`,`https://www.shacknews.com/article/151271/all-bottles-the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time`),f=c(`bottle-locations`,`Nintendo Insider · Alex Seedhouse · bottle locations`,`https://www.nintendo-insider.com/zelda-ocarina-of-time-remake-bottle-locations-guide/`,`firsthand-guide`),p=c(`epona`,`Shacknews · Epona`,`https://www.shacknews.com/article/151270/how-to-get-epona-the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time`),m=c(`biggoron`,`Shacknews · Biggoron trading quest`,`https://www.shacknews.com/article/151276/how-to-get-biggorons-sword-the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time`),h=c(`hall`,`Shacknews · Hall of Fallen Foes`,`https://www.shacknews.com/article/151277/where-to-find-the-hall-of-fallen-foes-the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time`),g=c(`songs`,`ZeldaCentral · remake songbook reference`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/ocarina-songs/`),_=c(`capacity`,`ZeldaCentral · remake capacity upgrades`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/equipment-upgrades/`),v=c(`masks`,`ZeldaCentral · Happy Mask Shopkeeper route`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/mask-guide/`),y=c(`thoughts`,`ZeldaCentral · Fairy’s Thoughts reference`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/fairys-thoughts/`),b=c(`summit-fairy`,`ZeldaCentral · summit fairy and magic meter`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/walkthrough/death-mountain-summit-and-crater/`),x=c(`castle-fairy`,`ZeldaCentral · castle fairy and Spin Attack`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/walkthrough/bombchu-bowling-and-spin-attack/`),S=c(`zora-fairy`,`ZeldaCentral · Zora’s Fountain fairy`,`https://zeldacentral.com/games/ocarina-of-time-remake/walkthrough/lord-jabu-jabus-belly/`),C=c(`nintendo`,`Nintendo · official Switch 2 game overview`,`https://www.nintendo.com/us/store/products/the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-switch-2/`,`official`,null),w=c(`trailer`,`Nintendo · ocarina microphone and rematches`,`https://www.nintendo.com/us/whatsnew/you-have-been-summoned-to-watch-the-new-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-overview-trailer/`,`official`,`2026-10-14`),T=(e,t,n,...r)=>({id:e,title:t,text:n,evidence:r.map(({id:e})=>e)}),E=[{slug:`five-bottles`,title:`All five bottles`,subtitle:`Room for another fairy.`,description:`Collect the remake’s extra Potion Shop bottle and the four other reusable bottles.`,category:`collection`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Access to Castle Town; later adult Link, Epona and the Fairy Bow`],reward:`Five reusable bottles`,steps:[T(`potion-shop`,`Catch the shopkeeper’s bug`,`In Castle Town’s Potion Shop, accept the bug-catching request. Use the lent bottle to catch the insect, then speak to the shopkeeper again to keep the bottle.`,d,f),T(`super-cuccos`,`Win Talon’s game`,`Wake Talon at Hyrule Castle first. At Lon Lon Ranch, enter the left building and pay 10 Rupees. Find the three Super Cuccos within 30 seconds; set aside ordinary birds you have checked. Win the milk bottle.`,d,f),T(`cuccos-ground`,`Round up the easy Cuccos`,`In Kakariko, check the construction site, village entrance, northern road and bouncing wooden crate near the central buildings. Carry each bird to the Cucco Lady’s pen. Roll into the crate to release its bird.`,f),T(`cucco-bricks`,`Reach the brick pile`,`Keep one Cucco in your hands. From the raised platform near the construction site, glide to the bird on the bricks. Throw both down safely and return them to the pen.`,f),T(`cuccos-windmill`,`Cross behind the windmill fence`,`Carry a Cucco to the windmill entrance and glide over the low fence. Throw the bird there and your transport bird back toward the village. Climb the ladders behind the windmill for the seventh bird.`,f),T(`cucco-bottle`,`Claim the Cucco Lady’s bottle`,`Return all seven Cuccos to the pen and speak to their owner. Ask her for a location hint if one is missing.`,f,d),T(`rutos-letter`,`Keep Ruto’s letter bottle`,`Win the Silver Scale in Zora’s Domain. Dive through its Lake Hylia tunnel and retrieve the bottle underwater near the exit. Show King Zora the letter to keep the bottle.`,d,f),T(`poe-bottle`,`Sell five Big Poes`,`Bring Epona, the Fairy Bow and empty bottles to Hyrule Field as an adult. Jump the purple-lit obstacles, shoot the Big Poes and bottle their spirits. Sell five to the ruined-market Poe Collector: 500 points earns the bottle.`,d,f,l)],changes:[`The Potion Shop request adds a bottle absent from the N64 game.`,`The Poe bottle arrives at 500 points. The 1,000-point prize is a Gold Rupee.`],notes:[`Bottle numbers are a checklist order. Keep an empty bottle ready for quest items or supplies.`],sources:[d,f,l]},{slug:`songs-and-ocarina`,title:`Songs & the ocarina`,subtitle:`Twelve melodies. One of your own.`,description:`Find the twelve fixed songs, restore the Scarecrow Song and use the remake’s ocarina controls.`,category:`quest`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Fairy Ocarina; later Ocarina of Time and access to both ages`],reward:`Twelve fixed songs · Scarecrow Song`,steps:[T(`first-ocarina`,`Accept Saria’s instrument`,`Leave Kokiri Forest after Gohma; Saria gives you the Fairy Ocarina on the bridge.`,l),T(`lullaby`,`Zelda’s Lullaby`,`Meet Zelda, then learn the royal melody from Impa in the castle courtyard.`,g),T(`sun`,`Sun’s Song`,`Play the Lullaby before the Royal Family’s Tomb in Kakariko Graveyard. Read the tablet inside.`,g),T(`epona-song`,`Epona’s Song`,`Show your ocarina to Malon in Lon Lon Ranch’s paddock.`,g,p),T(`saria-song`,`Saria’s Song`,`Follow the Lost Woods music to Saria in the Sacred Forest Meadow.`,g),T(`time`,`Song of Time`,`Retrieve Zelda’s ocarina from the castle moat; learn the melody in her message.`,g),T(`storms`,`Song of Storms`,`As an adult, show your ocarina to the windmill musician in Kakariko.`,g),T(`minuet`,`Minuet of Forest`,`Meet Sheik in the adult Sacred Forest Meadow before the Forest Temple.`,g),T(`prelude`,`Prelude of Light`,`After the Forest Temple, return to Sheik in the Temple of Time.`,g,l),T(`bolero`,`Bolero of Fire`,`Reach Death Mountain Crater through adult Goron City and meet Sheik.`,g),T(`serenade`,`Serenade of Water`,`Learn Sheik’s melody after obtaining the Iron Boots in the Ice Cavern.`,g),T(`nocturne`,`Nocturne of Shadow`,`Return to Kakariko after the Water Temple and meet Sheik.`,g,l),T(`requiem`,`Requiem of Spirit`,`Cross the desert to the Colossus and approach the Spirit Temple to meet Sheik.`,g,l),T(`scarecrow`,`Restore your Scarecrow Song`,`Teach Bonooru a memorable tune at Lake Hylia as a child. Replay it to him as an adult. Use it at supported spots to summon a scarecrow for the Hookshot.`,g),T(`input`,`Choose buttons or microphone`,`Follow the notes in the ocarina’s songbook. You can also hum or play a melody Link knows into the Switch 2 microphone.`,C,w)],changes:[`The remake supports microphone input as well as buttons.`],notes:[`Use the in-game staff for the current controller prompts. The Scarecrow Song is your own tune, separate from the twelve fixed melodies.`],sources:[g,l,p,C,w]},{slug:`epona`,title:`Win Epona`,subtitle:`A friend across seven years.`,description:`Learn her song, beat Ingo twice and escape Lon Lon Ranch with Epona.`,category:`quest`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Wake Talon as a child`,`Epona’s Song`,`Adult Link`,`Rupees for riding and races`],reward:`Epona · optional Lon Lon Cow`,steps:[T(`child-friend`,`Learn her song as a child`,`After waking Talon, speak to Malon among the ranch’s horses. Show your ocarina and repeat Epona’s Song.`,p),T(`ride`,`Choose Epona as an adult`,`Visit the ranch by day and pay Ingo to ride. Play Epona’s Song in the paddock. Mount Epona before speaking to him again.`,p,l),T(`first-race`,`Win the first race`,`Challenge Ingo while mounted. Start pressing the gallop button before the race begins, take the inside line and use carrots to accelerate.`,p),T(`second-race`,`Win again and escape`,`Beat Ingo a second time. When he locks the gate, approach the low eastern fence at a gallop and jump it.`,p),T(`cow`,`Bring a cow home`,`After Talon returns to the ranch, ask Malon about the obstacle course. Finish in under 40 seconds for a cow at Link’s Kokiri home. Play Epona’s Song beside it with an empty bottle for milk.`,l)],changes:[`Epona also triggers the remake’s purple-marked Big Poe encounters.`],notes:[`The cow challenge is optional.`],sources:[p,l,d]},{slug:`biggoron-trade`,title:`Biggoron’s Sword`,subtitle:`One delivery after another.`,description:`Complete the adult trading chain with the remake’s longer delivery timers.`,category:`quest`,era:`Adult Link`,prerequisites:[`Epona`,`King Zora thawed with Blue Fire`,`Sun’s Song recommended`],reward:`Biggoron’s Sword`,steps:[T(`egg`,`Get the Pocket Egg`,`Speak to Kakariko’s Cucco Lady as an adult. Let her Pocket Egg hatch; the Sun’s Song advances time.`,m),T(`cojiro`,`Wake Talon and collect Cojiro`,`Use the Pocket Cucco beside sleeping Talon in Kakariko. Free Epona and speak to Talon again if he has not gone back to the ranch. Trade the happy Cucco to its owner for Cojiro.`,m),T(`mushroom`,`Start the mushroom delivery`,`Enter the Lost Woods from Kokiri and find the clearing with tree stumps near the entrance. Show Cojiro to the craftsman’s son by a stump for the Odd Mushroom. You have four minutes and cannot use ocarina warps.`,m,l),T(`poultice`,`Reach Granny`,`Ride to Kakariko. Go through the ordinary Potion Shop’s rear exit to reach Granny’s shop. Trade the mushroom for the Odd Poultice.`,m),T(`saw`,`Return to the woods`,`Bring the poultice to the same clearing. Give it to the Kokiri standing there for the Poacher’s Saw.`,m),T(`broken-sword`,`Find the master craftsman`,`Jump the broken bridge in Gerudo Valley on Epona. Trade the saw to the craftsman for the Broken Goron’s Sword.`,m),T(`prescription`,`Visit Biggoron`,`Show the broken sword to Biggoron at Death Mountain’s summit. Take his Prescription to the thawed King Zora.`,m),T(`frog`,`Deliver the Eyeball Frog`,`King Zora gives you the frog. Reach Lake Hylia Laboratory within 2:30 via the Domain’s underwater lake passage. Do not use ocarina warps.`,l),T(`drops`,`Rush back to the summit`,`Take the Eye Drops to Biggoron within 3:30. Ride through Hyrule Field to Kakariko, then climb Death Mountain. The Longshot can save time on the upper grates. Do not warp.`,l),T(`sword`,`Redeem the receipt`,`Give Biggoron the drops. Wait three days, then present his receipt for the sword. The Sun’s Song can speed up the wait.`,m,l)],changes:[`Remake delivery limits: mushroom 4:00; frog 2:30; drops 3:30.`],notes:[`The river and Death Mountain Magic Beans are optional shortcuts.`,`The sword is two-handed, so you cannot use a shield while wielding it.`],sources:[m,l]},{slug:`happy-mask-trade`,title:`The Happy Mask trade`,subtitle:`Four customers and a strange reward.`,description:`Sell four borrowed masks, repay the shop and claim the Deku capacity rewards.`,category:`quest`,era:`Child Link`,prerequisites:[`Show Zelda’s Letter to Kakariko’s gate guard`,`Happy Mask Shop open`],reward:`Mask of Truth · mask loans · Deku bag rewards`,steps:[T(`keaton`,`Sell the Keaton Mask`,`Borrow it in daylight. Wear it for Kakariko’s Death Mountain gate guard, sell it, then repay 10 Rupees at the shop.`,v),T(`skull`,`Use and sell the Skull Mask`,`Visit the Forest Stage before selling: from the Lost Woods entrance go right, left, right, left, left and enter the grass-hidden grotto. Wear the mask onstage for the top stick bag. Sell it to the lone Skull Kid and repay 20 Rupees.`,v,u),T(`spooky`,`Find the little gravekeeper`,`Sell the Spooky Mask to the child in Kakariko Graveyard during daylight. Repay 30 Rupees.`,v),T(`bunny`,`Catch the Running Man`,`Follow the runner circling Hyrule Field until he stops. Wear the Bunny Hood and sell it. Repay 50 Rupees.`,v,u),T(`truth`,`Claim the Mask of Truth`,`After repaying all four loans, take the Mask of Truth. The Goron, Zora and Gerudo masks also become available to borrow.`,v,u),T(`nut-bag`,`Return to the Forest Stage`,`Wear the Mask of Truth for the stage’s Deku Scrubs. Talk to the large Scrub for the top nut bag.`,u,l)],changes:[`The Mask of Truth reveals character thoughts and Gossip Stone hints.`],notes:[`You can reborrow the Skull Mask if you sold it before visiting the Forest Stage.`,`The 2027 amiibo masks are separate from this trade.`],sources:[v,u,l,C]},{slug:`capacity-upgrades`,title:`Bags, wallets & scales`,subtitle:`Carry a little more courage.`,description:`Collect the inventory upgrades using the remake’s prizes and limits.`,category:`quest`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Slingshot; later Bomb Bag, Fairy Bow and Epona`,`Mask trade for the final Deku upgrades`],reward:`1,000-Rupee wallet · 40 bombs · 50 seeds · 50 arrows · larger Deku bags · Golden Scale`,steps:[T(`wallet-500`,`Adult’s Wallet: 500 Rupees`,`Reach ten Skulltula tokens and claim the House of Skulltula reward in Kakariko.`,_),T(`wallet-1000`,`Giant’s Wallet: 1,000 Rupees`,`Return to the same family at thirty tokens. Claim any earlier outstanding rewards first.`,_,u),T(`seeds-40`,`Carry 40 seeds`,`As a child, score 10/10 in Castle Town’s Shooting Gallery.`,_),T(`seeds-50`,`Carry 50 seeds`,`Turn right at the Lost Woods entrance. Hit the target’s center three times.`,u,l),T(`bombs-30`,`Carry 30 bombs`,`Stop the rolling Goron with a bomb beside his challenge sign in Goron City, then speak to him.`,_),T(`bombs-40`,`Carry 40 bombs`,`Win Bombchu Bowling twice in Castle Town. The second victory awards the largest bag.`,_),T(`arrows-40`,`Carry 40 arrows`,`As an adult, hit all ten targets at Kakariko’s Shooting Gallery.`,_),T(`arrows-50`,`Carry 50 arrows`,`Bring Epona and the bow to Gerudo Fortress’s archery range. Score 1,400 to win the top quiver.`,_,u),T(`sticks-20`,`Carry 20 Deku Sticks`,`Reflect the Lost Woods Business Scrub’s shots, then buy its stick upgrade for 40 Rupees.`,_),T(`sticks-30`,`Carry 30 Deku Sticks`,`Wear the Skull Mask for the Forest Stage Scrubs and claim their reward.`,u,l),T(`nuts`,`Collect both nut upgrades`,`Bomb open the Lost Woods grotto near the meadow; buy the Scrub’s upgrade for 40 Rupees. Then wear the Mask of Truth at the Forest Stage for the 40-nut bag.`,u,_),T(`gold-scale`,`Win the Golden Scale`,`As an adult, fish at Lake Hylia. Aim for a catch at least 65 cm long and present it to the keeper.`,l)],changes:[`Wallet capacities are 200, 500 and 1,000 Rupees.`,`The top horseback-archery quiver requires 1,400 points in this remake.`],notes:[`The Silver Scale comes from the Zora diving game. The Happy Mask chapter explains how to reach the Forest Stage.`,`Heart Pieces and Skulltula locations have their own checklists.`],sources:[_,u,l]},{slug:`great-fairy-gifts`,title:`The six Great Fairy gifts`,subtitle:`Magic has a price this time.`,description:`Visit each fountain with the right equipment and enough Rupees for its offering.`,category:`quest`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Zelda’s Lullaby`,`Bombs; later Hammer and Golden Gauntlets`,`Rupees for the offerings`],reward:`Three spells · enhanced Spin Attack · doubled magic · halved damage`,steps:[T(`din`,`Summit: magic and Din’s Fire`,`As a child, bomb the fountain entrance beside the summit owl. Play Zelda’s Lullaby on the crest and offer 25 Rupees for the meter and spell.`,b,l),T(`spin`,`Castle: enhanced Spin Attack`,`Climb past the child castle gate and bomb the blocked fountain entrance. Play the Lullaby and offer 50 Rupees.`,x,l),T(`farore`,`Zora’s Fountain: Farore’s Wind`,`Bomb the cracked rock beyond Jabu-Jabu. Play the Lullaby and offer 100 Rupees for dungeon warp-point magic.`,S,l),T(`double-magic`,`Crater: doubled magic`,`As an adult, hammer the boulders blocking the fountain in Death Mountain Crater. Play the Lullaby and offer 200 Rupees.`,l),T(`nayru`,`Colossus: Nayru’s Love`,`At the Desert Colossus, bomb the wall between the palms. Enter, play the Lullaby and offer 300 Rupees for the barrier spell.`,l,u),T(`defense`,`Castle ruins: halved damage`,`With the Golden Gauntlets, leave the final castle across the rainbow bridge. Lift the huge block outside and offer 500 Rupees at the fountain after the Lullaby.`,l)],changes:[`Din’s Fire is at Death Mountain’s summit. The child castle fountain gives the enhanced Spin Attack.`,`The six offerings are 25, 50, 100, 200, 300 and 500 Rupees.`],notes:[`Temple tools and the gauntlets are recorded in the story chapters.`],sources:[b,x,S,l,u]},{slug:`remake-discoveries`,title:`Hall & fairy discoveries`,subtitle:`Some secrets remember another time.`,description:`Find the Hall of Fallen Foes, challenge defeated bosses and recognize the new fairy clues.`,category:`quest`,era:`Both ages`,prerequisites:[`Return to childhood after the Forest Temple for the Hall introduction`,`Navi for Fairy’s Thoughts`],reward:`Boss rematches · optional gauntlets · fairy hints`,steps:[T(`hall-unlock`,`Find the Hall introduction`,`After first returning to childhood, head to Kakariko and speak to Kaepora Gaebora outside the village. Then sleep in a bed, such as Link’s, to enter the Hall.`,h),T(`hall-statues`,`Study and challenge foes`,`Inspect defeated enemies’ statues and choose an available rematch. Use a silver owl statue for a boss gauntlet. Talk to Kaepora Gaebora to leave.`,h,C),T(`hall-gauntlets`,`Finish the optional gauntlets`,`Health carries between fights. Spend the Rupees offered before each battle carefully on supplies. Completing the child and adult boss rushes adds trophies to Link’s bedroom.`,h,l),T(`fairy-thoughts`,`Follow Navi’s fairy clues`,`When Navi pauses at a faint glow, approach and accept her prompt. Read each message. Some clues only pay off when you come back in the other age.`,y,C)],changes:[`The Hall adds rematches and gauntlets; Fairy’s Thoughts are a new kind of environmental clue.`],notes:[`This covers documented features and how to use them. It is not a complete list of new secrets, fairy messages or trophy conditions.`,`The cross-age Heart Piece follow-ups are in the Heart Piece checklist.`],sources:[h,y,l,C]}],D=`/ocarina-of-time-switch-2`,O=`${D}/map`,k=`Ocarina of Time Switch 2 walkthrough`,A=`A separate guide to the Nintendo Switch 2 remake: 14 story chapters, dungeon puzzles, bosses, 100 Gold Skulltulas, 36 Heart Pieces and side quests, with saved checklists and dated sources.`,j=[...e,...t,...s,...E],M=e=>j.find(t=>t.slug===e),N=e=>`${D}/${e}`;export{k as a,D as i,A as n,M as o,O as r,N as s,j as t};